WEBVTT

1
00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:21.413
Get ready for the feel,
the feel of real. X1.

2
00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.254
No pain, no gain.

3
00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:46.541
Pizza, guys.

4
00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:53.682
Whoo-hoo!

5
00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:09.595
Hello, Wade.

6
00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:11.326
Hello, Mrs. Gilmore.

7
00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:14.231
What's the matter?
Life getting you down?

8
00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:21.435
I was born in 2027.

9
00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:25.248
After the Corn Syrup Droughts,
after the Bandwidth Riots.

10
00:02:25.249 --> 00:02:27.445
After people stopped trying
to fix problems

11
00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:29.747
and just tried
to outlive them.

12
00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.792
My parents, they didn't make it
through those times,

13
00:02:38.793 --> 00:02:42.761
so I live here in Columbus, Ohio,
with my Aunt Alice.

14
00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:48.100
In 2045, Columbus is the
fastest-growing city on Earth.

15
00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:51.441
It's where Halliday and Morrow
started Gregarious Games.

16
00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:58.709
These days,
reality is a bummer.

17
00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:00.681
Everyone is looking
for a way to escape,

18
00:03:00.682 --> 00:03:02.220
and that's why Halliday...

19
00:03:02.221 --> 00:03:05.045
That's why he was
such a hero to us.

20
00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:08.621
He showed us that we could go somewhere
without going anywhere at all.

21
00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:12.324
You don't need a destination

22
00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:14.055
when you're running on
an omnidirectional treadmill

23
00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.400
with quadraphonic,
pressure-sensitive underlay.

24
00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.730
James Halliday saw the future.

25
00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.466
And then he built it.

26
00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.635
He gave us a place to go.

27
00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:25.966
A place called

28
00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:27.412
the OASIS.

29
00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.920
This is the OASIS.

30
00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:47.092
It's a place where the limits of
reality are your own imagination.

31
00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:02.636
You can do anything...

32
00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:04.680
...go anywhere.

33
00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:07.906
Like the vacation planet.

34
00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:10.716
Surf a 50-foot monster wave
in Hawaii.

35
00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:13.617
You can ski down the pyramids.

36
00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.520
You can climb Mount Everest

37
00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:17.021
with Batman.

38
00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:23.356
Check out this place.
It's a casino the size of a planet.

39
00:04:23.363 --> 00:04:25.032
You can lose your money there.

40
00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:27.431
You can get married.
You can get divorced.

41
00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:31.270
You can...
You can go in there.

42
00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:34.371
People come to the OASIS for
all the things they can do,

43
00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:37.544
but they stay because of all
the things they can be.

44
00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:42.814
Tall, beautiful, scary,
a different sex,

45
00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:46.045
a different species,
live-action, cartoon.

46
00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:48.654
It's all your call.

47
00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:51.985
Yeah, that's me.
Well, that's my avatar.

48
00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:55.961
At least, until I feel
like changing it.

49
00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:58.402
Except for eating, sleeping,
and bathroom breaks,

50
00:04:58.403 --> 00:05:02.467
whatever people wanna do,
they do it in the OASIS.

51
00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:05.468
And since everyone is here,
this is where we meet each other.

52
00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:06.811
It's where we make friends.

53
00:05:06.812 --> 00:05:09.136
Locate Aech.

54
00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:11.482
Locating Aech.

55
00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.348
Aech located.

56
00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:19.649
Sector 12. Planet Doom.

57
00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:22.992
Planet Doom, the most
dangerous place in the OASIS,

58
00:05:22.993 --> 00:05:26.089
and a pretty great place
to pick up coin.

59
00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:27.692
Figures Aech would be there.

60
00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:33.765
Aech is my best friend
in the OASIS.

61
00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:36.435
He's my best friend, period.

62
00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:39.336
Even though I've never actually
met him in the real world.

63
00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:45.506
- WADWhat's up, Aech?
- Hey, what up, Z?

64
00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:47.949
Next race is in 20 minutes,
and I can't do the late one.

65
00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:49.647
What the hell are you up to?

66
00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:52.284
Man, gettin' my kills on, bro.

67
00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:53.515
Is that Daito?

68
00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:55.119
Daito and Sho.

69
00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:02.994
This an artifact hunt?

70
00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:05.295
Yup. Gregarious 120.

71
00:06:05.298 --> 00:06:09.868
Turn into any giant robot
for two minutes. That's rad.

72
00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:11.239
Artifacts.

73
00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:14.840
Those were key.

74
00:06:14.841 --> 00:06:17.011
Halliday made sure
the OASIS was littered

75
00:06:17.012 --> 00:06:19.709
with enough
randomly powerful stuff

76
00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:24.082
that anyone could win
if they had the skills.

77
00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:26.921
Death matches and artifact hunts
are a good way to coin-snatch,

78
00:06:26.922 --> 00:06:29.688
but depending on your level
of armor, they're risky.

79
00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:33.525
You see,
everyone starts the same,

80
00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:34.986
but the more coin you make...

81
00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:37.162
- Mom! Mom!
- ...the more you level up.

82
00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:39.073
If you get killed, your avatar
can come back to life...

83
00:06:39.074 --> 00:06:40.365
Go get your dad!

84
00:06:40.366 --> 00:06:41.896
...but you lose
all your stuff.

85
00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:45.666
Everything you've
ever worked for.

86
00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:48.006
All your money.

87
00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:51.576
Your clothes.

88
00:06:53.112 --> 00:06:55.180
Your weapons.

89
00:06:55.181 --> 00:06:57.781
Since people spend most of
their time in the OASIS...

90
00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:02.460
...losing your shit means...

91
00:07:02.461 --> 00:07:05.085
Well, losing your shit.

92
00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:09.900
Aech, 10 minutes
until the race starts.

93
00:07:09.901 --> 00:07:12.096
AECOkay, Mom, I heard you.

94
00:07:12.098 --> 00:07:16.237
You see, the OASIS was the
brainchild of James Halliday.

95
00:07:16.238 --> 00:07:21.135
He and his partner, Ogden Morrow,
released the first OASIS build in 2025.

96
00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:25.410
It was an instant success, and
it made them both very rich.

97
00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:29.050
But Morrow was out of the picture
after a few years. And Halliday?

98
00:07:29.051 --> 00:07:32.388
He wasn't just the owner of
the world's biggest company.

99
00:07:32.389 --> 00:07:36.315
He was like a god.
People loved him.

100
00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:38.492
They worshiped him
as much as his creation.

101
00:07:38.493 --> 00:07:41.326
Maybe we should stop
talking about it

102
00:07:41.327 --> 00:07:43.827
and start, uh, showing it.

103
00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:46.130
If you all wanna reach
under your seats,

104
00:07:46.132 --> 00:07:48.470
you'll find that there's nothing there.

105
00:07:48.471 --> 00:07:52.668
But we're gonna... we're each
gonna bring you one now.

106
00:07:52.672 --> 00:07:56.808
And then,
on January 7, 2040...

107
00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:00.705
He died.

108
00:08:03.683 --> 00:08:05.603
And what he left behind

109
00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:08.885
changed everything.

110
00:08:21.367 --> 00:08:25.604
Hello. I am James Halliday.

111
00:08:25.605 --> 00:08:29.035
If you're watching this,
I'm dead.

112
00:08:29.041 --> 00:08:36.281
Before I died, I created what we
in the biz call an "Easter egg."

113
00:08:36.282 --> 00:08:43.192
A hidden object in a game that gives
special powers to whoever discovers it.

114
00:08:44.624 --> 00:08:47.192
The first person
to find the egg

115
00:08:47.193 --> 00:08:50.629
I've hidden somewhere
inside the OASIS

116
00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:54.466
will inherit my stock
in Gregarious Games,

117
00:08:54.467 --> 00:08:58.336
currently valued in excess
of half a million do...

118
00:08:58.337 --> 00:09:01.337
Uh, half a trillion
dollars' worth,

119
00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:07.810
and total control
of the OASIS itself.

120
00:09:07.813 --> 00:09:13.518
In the form of my avatar,
Anorak the All-Knowing,

121
00:09:13.519 --> 00:09:17.188
I created three keys.

122
00:09:17.189 --> 00:09:20.559
Three hidden challenges
test for worthy traits

123
00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:24.896
revealing three hidden keys
to three magic gates.

124
00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:29.067
And those with the skill
to survive these straits

125
00:09:29.068 --> 00:09:33.868
will reach the end,
where the prize awaits.

126
00:09:33.873 --> 00:09:36.443
Off you go, keys.

127
00:09:38.711 --> 00:09:43.715
The keys aren't just laying
around under a rock somewhere.

128
00:09:43.716 --> 00:09:46.446
I suppose you could say
they're invisible,

129
00:09:46.452 --> 00:09:50.188
hidden in a dark room
that's at the center of a maze

130
00:09:50.189 --> 00:09:53.159
that's located somewhere

131
00:09:54.093 --> 00:09:56.528
up here.

132
00:09:56.529 --> 00:10:00.629
Let the hunt
for Halliday's Easter egg

133
00:10:01.233 --> 00:10:02.534
begin.

134
00:10:08.774 --> 00:10:11.214
The challenge
is to find three keys,

135
00:10:11.215 --> 00:10:14.810
but in five years, no one
has even gotten one key.

136
00:10:14.814 --> 00:10:17.816
And the big scoreboard?
Still empty.

137
00:10:17.817 --> 00:10:19.747
Some long-forgotten gunter
cracked the first clue

138
00:10:19.752 --> 00:10:21.622
and found the first challenge.

139
00:10:21.623 --> 00:10:24.321
Then, this portal appeared.

140
00:10:24.323 --> 00:10:27.762
But the challenge to win the first
key was a race designed by Halliday

141
00:10:27.763 --> 00:10:30.760
that was so hard,
no one had ever finished it.

142
00:10:30.763 --> 00:10:34.273
The only ones still trying are the
gunters, as in "egg hunters,"

143
00:10:34.274 --> 00:10:37.836
like me and Sho and Daito,
and my best friend, Aech.

144
00:10:37.837 --> 00:10:41.637
Oh, and of course, the Sixers.

145
00:10:41.641 --> 00:10:42.811
The Sixers work for IOI...

146
00:10:42.812 --> 00:10:44.408
Sixers!

147
00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:46.144
...Innovative
Online Industries.

148
00:10:46.145 --> 00:10:47.605
They're the second-largest
company in the world

149
00:10:47.613 --> 00:10:49.851
with designs
on becoming the first.

150
00:10:49.852 --> 00:10:51.818
Which is why they're putting
everything they got

151
00:10:51.819 --> 00:10:53.147
into winning
Halliday's contest.

152
00:10:53.152 --> 00:10:54.852
Buckle up!

153
00:10:55.621 --> 00:10:57.856
Sit in!

154
00:10:57.857 --> 00:11:00.527
We call 'em "Sixers"
'cause that's the company rule.

155
00:11:00.528 --> 00:11:03.795
No name, just numbers.

156
00:11:03.796 --> 00:11:06.626
They have a support team
made up of Halliday scholars.

157
00:11:06.632 --> 00:11:09.339
Like me, they spend all their
time studying pop culture

158
00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:10.995
that Halliday
was obsessed with,

159
00:11:11.003 --> 00:11:13.013
trying to find clues
to solve the contest.

160
00:11:15.608 --> 00:11:18.538
They're just following
the orders of the head of IOI,

161
00:11:18.544 --> 00:11:21.684
this dickweed
named Nolan Sorrento.

162
00:11:27.653 --> 00:11:29.291
How'd you get here before me?

163
00:11:29.292 --> 00:11:31.718
Well, I didn't make a pit stop
at the hair salon.

164
00:11:31.724 --> 00:11:34.225
- What up, Z?
- What's up, Aech?

165
00:11:34.226 --> 00:11:35.526
Saved you a spot.

166
00:11:35.528 --> 00:11:36.895
Thanks, bro.

167
00:11:41.067 --> 00:11:42.634
I gotta go to the back.

168
00:11:42.635 --> 00:11:45.295
Ugh. So you can skim coins
from crashed cars?

169
00:11:45.304 --> 00:11:48.073
- That's just sad, man.
- Fuel's low.

170
00:11:48.074 --> 00:11:51.881
Oh, but you still had enough to pay
for that Something About Mary hairdo.

171
00:12:33.119 --> 00:12:34.219
First to the key.

172
00:12:35.521 --> 00:12:36.888
First to the egg!

173
00:13:26.071 --> 00:13:28.011
Aech, are you seeing this?

174
00:13:30.943 --> 00:13:33.181
Yeah, I see it.
That's Kaneda's bike from Akira.

175
00:13:33.182 --> 00:13:35.409
It's a licensed skin
over a standard frame.

176
00:13:35.414 --> 00:13:38.283
No, not the bike.
Forget the bike.

177
00:13:38.284 --> 00:13:40.124
The girl,
I think it's Art3mis.

178
00:13:40.125 --> 00:13:42.419
The Art3mis? The Sixer Fixer?

179
00:13:42.421 --> 00:13:45.359
I've seen all her walk-throughs,
her Twitch streams.

180
00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:47.327
It's her. It's definitely her.

181
00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:36.540
Go, go, go!
Get there! Come on!

182
00:15:42.308 --> 00:15:43.438
AECYou got it, you got it!

183
00:15:52.885 --> 00:15:54.315
Balls.

184
00:15:59.959 --> 00:16:01.029
She's not gonna make it.

185
00:16:03.762 --> 00:16:05.596
Bail! Bail out!

186
00:16:05.597 --> 00:16:06.667
Bail!

187
00:16:12.805 --> 00:16:14.505
Ow!

188
00:16:45.037 --> 00:16:46.537
Damn, I loved that bike.

189
00:16:46.538 --> 00:16:48.206
Oh, Aech could...

190
00:16:48.207 --> 00:16:50.507
Well, he's my friend,
but he could fix it for you.

191
00:16:57.850 --> 00:17:00.618
This is my workshop.
Touch nothing.

192
00:17:07.159 --> 00:17:09.289
Where did you find
an Iron Giant?

193
00:17:09.294 --> 00:17:12.163
Find it? I'm building it.
That's a commission.

194
00:17:12.164 --> 00:17:15.133
Oh, yeah. Aech is
top-rated on the mod boards.

195
00:17:15.134 --> 00:17:17.974
People all over the OASIS
pay him serious coin.

196
00:17:17.975 --> 00:17:20.338
Oh, hey, check this out!

197
00:17:20.339 --> 00:17:23.339
Hey. Z, yo.

198
00:17:23.342 --> 00:17:25.812
- The Galactica, of course.
- These are my babies, all right, man?

199
00:17:25.813 --> 00:17:27.578
Sulaco, from Aliens.

200
00:17:27.579 --> 00:17:30.179
Dude, how are you
showing off my shit?

201
00:17:30.182 --> 00:17:31.752
Valley Forge, from Silent Running.
Oh, where's the Harkonnen Drop-Ship?

202
00:17:31.753 --> 00:17:34.318
That thing is sick.
Folds space like a boss.

203
00:17:34.319 --> 00:17:36.389
I mean, you can get from Incipio
to Arrakis in three seconds...

204
00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:38.156
Fingers!

205
00:17:38.157 --> 00:17:39.587
You'll have to excuse him.

206
00:17:39.591 --> 00:17:41.731
He gets a little nervous
around pretty girls.

207
00:17:48.834 --> 00:17:51.344
I can fix it in 10 minutes.

208
00:17:52.671 --> 00:17:55.271
Yup. He's pretty great.

209
00:17:55.274 --> 00:17:58.344
I assume you and Shoulder
Blades are clanned up.

210
00:17:58.345 --> 00:18:00.611
Oh, Aech? Nah.

211
00:18:00.612 --> 00:18:05.582
I mean, he's really good,
but I don't clan.

212
00:18:05.584 --> 00:18:08.286
Oh, 'cause you're Parzival,

213
00:18:08.287 --> 00:18:10.857
as in the knight who found
the Holy Grail by himself.

214
00:18:10.858 --> 00:18:12.856
What about you, Art3mis?

215
00:18:12.858 --> 00:18:15.858
Goddess of the hunt. Clans must
be killing to sign you up.

216
00:18:17.429 --> 00:18:19.399
- Favorite shooter?
- Excuse me?

217
00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:21.368
James Halliday's
favorite first-person shooter.

218
00:18:21.369 --> 00:18:22.934
- What?
- Oh. GoldenEye.

219
00:18:22.935 --> 00:18:25.295
- Playing as?
- Oddjob. Is this a test?

220
00:18:25.304 --> 00:18:27.038
Favorite game variant?

221
00:18:27.039 --> 00:18:28.639
Game variant was "slappers only."
No weapons.

222
00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:30.310
I know what "slappers only" means.
Racer?

223
00:18:30.311 --> 00:18:32.609
Turbo. And his favorite food
was Hot Pockets.

224
00:18:32.611 --> 00:18:34.581
Favorite restaurant
was Chuck E Cheese.

225
00:18:34.582 --> 00:18:36.918
Song was Video Killed the
Radio Star by the Buggles.

226
00:18:36.919 --> 00:18:38.815
Video wTake on Me by A-ha.

227
00:18:38.817 --> 00:18:43.417
Oh, oh... His favorite
quote was from Superman.

228
00:18:43.422 --> 00:18:45.389
"Some people
can read War and Peace

229
00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:47.590
"and come away thinking it's
a simple adventure story..."

230
00:18:47.593 --> 00:18:50.063
"Others can read the ingredients on
the back of a chewing-gum wrapper

231
00:18:50.064 --> 00:18:53.131
"and unlock the secrets
of the universe."

232
00:18:53.132 --> 00:18:55.566
Lex Luthor.

233
00:18:55.567 --> 00:18:58.236
Cool.

234
00:18:58.237 --> 00:19:02.167
What would you do? If you won.
The whole contest, I mean.

235
00:19:02.174 --> 00:19:05.281
Oh! I mean, I've got tons
of plans in the real world.

236
00:19:05.282 --> 00:19:10.077
I'd... I'd move into a huge mansion,
buy a bunch of cool shit, not be poor.

237
00:19:11.283 --> 00:19:14.986
Now I know
why you stopped short.

238
00:19:14.987 --> 00:19:18.156
I stopped because of Kong.
No one ever makes it past Kong.

239
00:19:18.157 --> 00:19:20.426
That... That's...
That's, like, a rule.

240
00:19:20.427 --> 00:19:23.755
Well, then you know it can't be true.
Because Halliday hated making rules.

241
00:19:23.762 --> 00:19:25.496
I can't afford to zero out.

242
00:19:25.497 --> 00:19:27.297
- You're afraid to lose your shit.
- No, I'm not!

243
00:19:27.299 --> 00:19:28.869
What happens when IOI
offers you guaranteed coin

244
00:19:28.870 --> 00:19:30.267
for the keys to the kingdom?

245
00:19:30.269 --> 00:19:32.599
Nolan Sorrento
takes over the world.

246
00:19:32.604 --> 00:19:36.941
A real gunter would risk everything
to save the OASIS from IOI.

247
00:19:36.942 --> 00:19:38.442
Who said that?

248
00:19:38.443 --> 00:19:39.913
Me.

249
00:19:42.114 --> 00:19:44.215
There you go. Good as new.

250
00:19:44.216 --> 00:19:46.546
Thanks for the fix-up, my man.

251
00:19:56.228 --> 00:19:58.328
That's better.

252
00:19:58.330 --> 00:20:02.370
I'll wave to you
from the finish line, McFly.

253
00:20:05.704 --> 00:20:07.010
That went well.

254
00:20:07.011 --> 00:20:08.905
Thanks to you,
Captain Big Mouth.

255
00:20:08.907 --> 00:20:12.337
Wade? Wade?
Where the hell are my gloves?

256
00:20:12.344 --> 00:20:14.384
Shit. I gotta go.

257
00:20:17.316 --> 00:20:19.416
ANNOUNCEX1.

258
00:20:19.418 --> 00:20:22.388
When I'm after gold on Planet Doom,
I need every edge I can get.

259
00:20:22.389 --> 00:20:26.324
Every push, punch, gunshot,
you feel it all.

260
00:20:26.325 --> 00:20:30.655
Get ready for the feel,
the feel of real. X1.

261
00:20:30.662 --> 00:20:33.002
The X1 is like
wearing a second skin.

262
00:20:33.003 --> 00:20:34.998
A skin that kicks ass.

263
00:20:36.702 --> 00:20:39.609
I zeroed out 'cause
of your broke-ass gloves.

264
00:20:39.610 --> 00:20:41.035
Who told you to use them?

265
00:20:41.039 --> 00:20:43.179
You took hers.

266
00:20:44.209 --> 00:20:46.209
So you lost a death match.

267
00:20:46.211 --> 00:20:50.121
Why don't you just respawn and
level up like everyone else?

268
00:20:50.122 --> 00:20:52.275
You don't get it.

269
00:20:52.284 --> 00:20:54.524
I bought all these power-ups for
this challenge, and I lost it all.

270
00:20:54.525 --> 00:20:56.389
That artifact
was gonna pay for the house!

271
00:20:56.390 --> 00:20:58.055
Wait.

272
00:20:58.056 --> 00:21:02.056
How much of our house money
did you spend on upgrades?

273
00:21:02.060 --> 00:21:04.929
Well, all of it,
but I was gonna win.

274
00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:07.870
That was our ticket
out of here.

275
00:21:10.435 --> 00:21:11.965
You idiot.

276
00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:13.970
No, but I only lost 'cause
of the bad gloves.

277
00:21:13.972 --> 00:21:15.742
Our house! Our goddamn house!

278
00:21:15.743 --> 00:21:17.441
My boys
were in that challenge.

279
00:21:17.442 --> 00:21:19.752
You couldn't have beat them
in a bootsuit, you noob.

280
00:21:19.753 --> 00:21:22.905
Stop! No! No!

281
00:21:22.914 --> 00:21:24.220
Alice, call the police!

282
00:21:24.221 --> 00:21:25.876
No, we are not
calling the cops.

283
00:21:25.884 --> 00:21:27.752
Go to your room, Rick.

284
00:21:27.753 --> 00:21:30.087
Aw, come on, Alice.

285
00:21:30.088 --> 00:21:34.088
Why do you put up with this guy?
He's a shitshow.

286
00:21:34.092 --> 00:21:38.662
I ought to kick the both of you out.
I swear to G-O-D, Wade Watts,

287
00:21:38.664 --> 00:21:41.432
if I catch you
touching my stuff again,

288
00:21:41.433 --> 00:21:44.043
not joking... Out.

289
00:21:50.909 --> 00:21:53.244
"Wade Watts."

290
00:21:53.245 --> 00:21:55.005
My dad picked that name

291
00:21:55.013 --> 00:21:57.253
because it sounded
like a superhero's alter ego,

292
00:21:57.254 --> 00:22:00.918
like Peter Parker
or Bruce Banner.

293
00:22:00.919 --> 00:22:02.987
But he died when I was a kid.

294
00:22:02.988 --> 00:22:06.188
My mom, too,
and I ended up here,

295
00:22:06.191 --> 00:22:08.091
living with Aunt Alice

296
00:22:08.093 --> 00:22:10.533
and her endless string
of hard-loving losers.

297
00:22:13.332 --> 00:22:16.200
"Halliday hated making rules."

298
00:22:16.201 --> 00:22:18.871
Why is that line
sticking in my head?

299
00:22:21.173 --> 00:22:24.709
Maybe it's 'cause Art3mis
said it, and she's hot.

300
00:22:24.710 --> 00:22:26.980
Maybe it's because
she called me out,

301
00:22:26.981 --> 00:22:30.147
sitting here
in my tiny corner of nowhere,

302
00:22:30.148 --> 00:22:32.878
protecting my small slice
of nothing.

303
00:22:32.884 --> 00:22:35.152
Or maybe...

304
00:22:35.153 --> 00:22:37.663
Maybe it's because
that line means something

305
00:22:37.664 --> 00:22:39.356
and I missed it.

306
00:22:42.160 --> 00:22:43.730
The day the contest
was announced,

307
00:22:43.731 --> 00:22:46.059
the Halliday Journals
appeared.

308
00:22:46.064 --> 00:22:49.233
He told us to look in his brain.
This was the next best thing.

309
00:22:49.234 --> 00:22:52.741
At first, it was jammed with
gunters looking for answers.

310
00:22:52.742 --> 00:22:55.368
Now, the once-crowded halls
of Halliday's memories

311
00:22:55.374 --> 00:22:56.644
are left to people like me.

312
00:22:56.645 --> 00:22:59.410
Parzival. Oh, joy!

313
00:22:59.411 --> 00:23:02.911
And how will you eat up
my valuable search time today?

314
00:23:02.914 --> 00:23:05.084
Gregarious Games, 2029...
Office party.

315
00:23:05.085 --> 00:23:08.252
Office party. Yes, you've only
seen it a thousand times.

316
00:23:08.253 --> 00:23:11.021
Why not go back?

317
00:23:11.022 --> 00:23:14.729
Each entry into Halliday's
Journals is meticulously assembled

318
00:23:14.730 --> 00:23:17.226
from personal photographs,
home video recordings,

319
00:23:17.229 --> 00:23:19.159
surveillance, and nanny cams.

320
00:23:19.164 --> 00:23:23.003
All rendered into a three-dimensional
virtual experience.

321
00:23:23.004 --> 00:23:26.670
Also, Halliday archived every film,
game, book, and television program

322
00:23:26.671 --> 00:23:30.007
he ever saw,
located on the mezzanine.

323
00:23:30.008 --> 00:23:33.577
No weapons or mature-themed avatars
are permitted within the Journals.

324
00:23:33.578 --> 00:23:37.378
Please enjoy your time with us,
and happy gunting!

325
00:23:37.382 --> 00:23:39.220
I like cleaning up.

326
00:23:39.221 --> 00:23:41.647
Okay, Jim,
I'm, uh... I'm going.

327
00:23:46.558 --> 00:23:49.527
Everything changes, Jim.
Everything evolves.

328
00:23:49.528 --> 00:23:52.897
Some things are perfect
just the way they arAsteroids.

329
00:23:52.898 --> 00:23:56.968
People don't live inside
an Asteroids arcade cabinet.

330
00:23:58.270 --> 00:24:00.137
I know that.

331
00:24:00.138 --> 00:24:02.368
Yeah, well, people are living
inside the arcade we built.

332
00:24:02.374 --> 00:24:04.542
- I built.
- Uh, well...

333
00:24:04.543 --> 00:24:07.244
Right. Well, I guess you
can say whatever you want.

334
00:24:07.245 --> 00:24:08.775
I don't really wanna
talk about it anymore.

335
00:24:08.780 --> 00:24:09.950
No, of course
you don't wanna talk about it.

336
00:24:09.951 --> 00:24:11.378
You're forcing me out.

337
00:24:11.383 --> 00:24:12.917
Closer on Halliday.

338
00:24:12.918 --> 00:24:14.788
Look, invention
comes with responsibilities

339
00:24:14.789 --> 00:24:16.954
you didn't ask for.

340
00:24:16.955 --> 00:24:19.155
All right, if you make
something people want or need

341
00:24:19.157 --> 00:24:21.957
then it's up to you to set the limits.
You have to make some rules.

342
00:24:21.960 --> 00:24:23.560
"I don't wanna
make any more rules."

343
00:24:23.562 --> 00:24:25.402
I don't wanna make
any more rules.

344
00:24:25.403 --> 00:24:26.827
"I'm a dreamer."

345
00:24:26.832 --> 00:24:28.132
I'm a dreamer.

346
00:24:28.133 --> 00:24:31.068
- I build worlds.
- "I build worlds."

347
00:24:31.069 --> 00:24:33.838
We created something beautiful,
Jim, but it's changed.

348
00:24:33.839 --> 00:24:35.469
Okay? It's really
not a game anymore.

349
00:24:35.474 --> 00:24:37.107
Are we finished?

350
00:24:37.108 --> 00:24:41.648
I liked how things were
when they were...

351
00:24:43.081 --> 00:24:45.249
When it was a game.

352
00:24:45.250 --> 00:24:48.020
And we're back to where we started.
But that's the point, isn't it?

353
00:24:48.021 --> 00:24:50.519
Things move forward
whether you like it or not.

354
00:24:50.522 --> 00:24:52.656
Yeah, we're finished.

355
00:24:52.657 --> 00:24:54.357
Fine.

356
00:24:56.528 --> 00:25:00.368
Why can't we
go backwards, for once?

357
00:25:02.667 --> 00:25:06.867
Backwards, really fast.
Fast as we can.

358
00:25:06.872 --> 00:25:08.972
Really put the pedal to
the metal, you know?

359
00:25:08.974 --> 00:25:11.675
Go back 10 seconds!

360
00:25:11.676 --> 00:25:16.306
Why can't we go backwards,
for once?

361
00:25:16.314 --> 00:25:20.718
Backwards, really fast.
Fast as we can.

362
00:25:20.719 --> 00:25:23.519
Really put the pedal to
the metal, you know?

363
00:25:24.523 --> 00:25:26.323
Bill and Ted did it.

364
00:25:47.646 --> 00:25:49.706
Back again so soon?

365
00:25:51.249 --> 00:25:53.449
Careful not to lose your shit.

366
00:25:57.489 --> 00:25:59.857
You figured something out.

367
00:25:59.858 --> 00:26:02.088
Parzival, tell me.

368
00:27:42.160 --> 00:27:46.997
Nice racing, Padawan.
You're the first to finish.

369
00:27:46.998 --> 00:27:51.538
Mr. Halliday... Anorak.

370
00:27:52.871 --> 00:27:54.438
It's such an honor.

371
00:27:54.439 --> 00:27:56.739
The honor is all mine.

372
00:28:07.819 --> 00:28:09.619
Get yourself a clue.

373
00:28:24.135 --> 00:28:27.735
Who is this Parzival,
and how the hell is he winning?

374
00:28:27.739 --> 00:28:30.377
Well, here's a better question.
Who cares?

375
00:28:30.378 --> 00:28:32.475
Halliday's contest
is vitally important.

376
00:28:32.477 --> 00:28:35.577
I mean, it's nothing less than a
war for control of the future.

377
00:28:35.580 --> 00:28:38.816
But this Parzival?
He's not even clanned up.

378
00:28:38.817 --> 00:28:42.147
He's alone. We have an army.

379
00:28:42.153 --> 00:28:43.893
And yet,
he's got the first key.

380
00:28:43.894 --> 00:28:45.756
Yeah, he has a key,

381
00:28:45.757 --> 00:28:48.757
but you have to get three
of 'em to win the contest.

382
00:28:48.760 --> 00:28:51.428
Our stock dove 6% yesterday.

383
00:28:51.429 --> 00:28:55.399
Loyalty division is reporting
profits of 28%. F'Nale.

384
00:28:55.400 --> 00:28:58.240
We're opening five new
loyalty centers this month.

385
00:28:58.241 --> 00:29:00.266
Debt Services dwarfs Hardware.

386
00:29:00.271 --> 00:29:02.341
Now, you really wanna talk
to me about stock prices?

387
00:29:02.342 --> 00:29:04.374
The shareholders
won't be happy.

388
00:29:04.375 --> 00:29:07.044
It's not our job to make them happy.
It's our job to make them money,

389
00:29:07.045 --> 00:29:11.145
but once we launch this little
baby, they're gonna flip.

390
00:29:12.417 --> 00:29:15.617
We call this Pure O2.

391
00:29:15.620 --> 00:29:17.520
This is the first
of our planned upgrades.

392
00:29:17.522 --> 00:29:20.132
Once we can roll back some of
Halliday's ad restrictions,

393
00:29:20.133 --> 00:29:24.194
we estimate
we can sell up to 80%

394
00:29:24.195 --> 00:29:29.595
of an individual's visual field before
inducing seizures, so picture this...

395
00:29:29.601 --> 00:29:32.671
All of this implies
we win the contest.

396
00:29:35.573 --> 00:29:37.741
Indeed, it does.

397
00:29:39.544 --> 00:29:42.312
Dude, you won the key
and 100,000 coins?

398
00:29:42.313 --> 00:29:43.819
As soon as I took the key,

399
00:29:43.820 --> 00:29:45.715
all the coins
just appeared in my account.

400
00:29:45.717 --> 00:29:48.047
I'll tell you what, I'm
soiling my haptics right now.

401
00:29:51.656 --> 00:29:53.456
What the hell's a Cataclyst?

402
00:29:53.458 --> 00:29:57.227
A bomb. Kills every avatar
on a planet, even the owner.

403
00:29:57.228 --> 00:29:58.458
Who'd want that?

404
00:29:58.463 --> 00:30:00.533
IOI.
They buy everything.

405
00:30:01.833 --> 00:30:04.635
Twenty-thou
for the holy hand grenade?

406
00:30:04.636 --> 00:30:06.366
That's a steal!

407
00:30:08.640 --> 00:30:12.476
Whoa! Zemeckis Cube!
I need one of those.

408
00:30:12.477 --> 00:30:14.207
Okay, don't spend
all your money.

409
00:30:17.816 --> 00:30:20.186
X1 haptic bootsuit.

410
00:30:34.766 --> 00:30:36.226
Oh, yeah!

411
00:31:29.220 --> 00:31:32.420
i-R0k, old friend.
How are you?

412
00:31:34.592 --> 00:31:36.262
To be honest,
I have kind of a neck thing.

413
00:31:36.263 --> 00:31:38.230
It's like a carpel-tunnel deal

414
00:31:38.231 --> 00:31:40.099
but with your neck,
if that's even a thing.

415
00:31:40.100 --> 00:31:42.728
So if you could just stand
to... to your right.

416
00:31:42.734 --> 00:31:44.004
My right, your left.

417
00:31:45.870 --> 00:31:49.240
Thanks, it's the repetitive stress.
Oh.

418
00:31:50.275 --> 00:31:51.435
Here he is.

419
00:31:53.511 --> 00:31:58.515
The steampunk pirate king.
I knew him well, Sorrento.

420
00:31:58.516 --> 00:32:00.886
There are only three things
in this world I hate,

421
00:32:00.887 --> 00:32:04.855
steampunk, pirates,
and tabbouleh.

422
00:32:04.856 --> 00:32:07.686
I mean,
why do they even have it?

423
00:32:07.692 --> 00:32:10.394
Is there a reason
we're meeting here?

424
00:32:10.395 --> 00:32:15.625
Yes, Nolan. The Orb of Osuvox.

425
00:32:15.633 --> 00:32:19.003
You wanted it. He had it.
And so here it is.

426
00:32:22.774 --> 00:32:26.743
It creates an impenetrable magic
shield that can only be taken down

427
00:32:26.744 --> 00:32:29.112
by a magic spell.

428
00:32:29.113 --> 00:32:31.548
The Orb of Osuvox.

429
00:32:31.549 --> 00:32:32.949
Don't say that again.

430
00:32:32.951 --> 00:32:34.051
Okay.

431
00:32:36.220 --> 00:32:39.920
Now, I'm gonna need you
to keep this for now.

432
00:32:39.924 --> 00:32:42.164
I'm gonna let you know
when I wanna use it.

433
00:32:42.165 --> 00:32:43.230
Okay?

434
00:32:46.631 --> 00:32:50.667
Right now, though,
I have another job for you.

435
00:32:50.668 --> 00:32:51.998
Ah.

436
00:32:52.003 --> 00:32:53.937
Parzival.

437
00:32:53.938 --> 00:32:56.908
Let me guess, you want
him off the scoreboard.

438
00:32:57.742 --> 00:32:59.242
Can you do that?

439
00:32:59.243 --> 00:33:01.778
Well, he's a superstar.

440
00:33:01.779 --> 00:33:03.649
He made it
through the first gate

441
00:33:03.650 --> 00:33:06.248
and avatars are gonna be
on him like hoes on Santa.

442
00:33:06.250 --> 00:33:09.486
i-R0k, how much more
do you want?

443
00:33:09.487 --> 00:33:13.117
That's what I like about you, Nolan.
You never lick.

444
00:33:13.124 --> 00:33:15.164
You bite straight
to the chocolaty center

445
00:33:15.165 --> 00:33:17.294
of the Tootsie Pop.

446
00:33:17.295 --> 00:33:19.695
Remember that old commercial,
with the owl?

447
00:33:19.697 --> 00:33:20.767
i-R0k.

448
00:33:22.700 --> 00:33:24.500
Three times my normal fee.

449
00:33:24.502 --> 00:33:26.136
Done.

450
00:33:26.137 --> 00:33:28.007
Wait, really?
I should have asked for five.

451
00:33:28.008 --> 00:33:30.006
Is four still on the table?

452
00:33:32.210 --> 00:33:35.210
There's five of us
on the big board now.

453
00:33:35.213 --> 00:33:38.015
Art3mis was next,
no surprise there.

454
00:33:38.016 --> 00:33:41.346
She was on the track when I won.
She saw me going backwards.

455
00:33:41.352 --> 00:33:46.392
I gave Aech a tip, made him promise not
to say anything, and then he won next.

456
00:33:46.393 --> 00:33:49.061
I'm pretty sure
he bragged to our pal Daito,

457
00:33:49.062 --> 00:33:51.795
'cause he won right after.

458
00:33:51.796 --> 00:33:55.396
And of course, Daito told
his best friend, Sho...

459
00:33:55.400 --> 00:33:57.534
He totally totaled his car,

460
00:33:57.535 --> 00:33:59.695
but then Sho got it, too.

461
00:34:08.679 --> 00:34:10.917
"A creator who hates
his own creation.

462
00:34:10.918 --> 00:34:15.415
"A hidden key, a leap not taken.
Retrace your steps, escape your past."

463
00:34:15.420 --> 00:34:18.155
"A creator who hates
his own creation.

464
00:34:18.156 --> 00:34:22.586
"A hidden key, a leap not taken.
Retrace your steps, escape your past.

465
00:34:22.593 --> 00:34:25.063
"And the key of jade
will be yours at last."

466
00:35:06.904 --> 00:35:08.874
"Escape your past."

467
00:35:12.543 --> 00:35:15.513
What part of your past are you
trying to escape, Halliday?

468
00:35:27.325 --> 00:35:29.085
- Hey, it's Parzival!
- Dude!

469
00:35:30.561 --> 00:35:32.095
You're, like,
totally my hero!

470
00:35:32.096 --> 00:35:33.256
Hey, Parzival!
Over here!

471
00:35:33.264 --> 00:35:35.398
Dude, you're amazing!

472
00:35:35.399 --> 00:35:37.680
Hey, Parzival! Right here!
Let me get an autograph!

473
00:35:43.474 --> 00:35:45.308
Watch it!

474
00:35:45.309 --> 00:35:49.446
You're famous now! You can't
just go wherever you want!

475
00:35:49.447 --> 00:35:50.847
No, no, no, I...

476
00:35:55.486 --> 00:35:57.656
Huh?

477
00:36:01.125 --> 00:36:03.525
Ahh!

478
00:36:09.600 --> 00:36:13.800
That is... That is not funny.

479
00:36:13.804 --> 00:36:16.473
Oh, God.

480
00:36:16.474 --> 00:36:19.109
Ugh.

481
00:36:19.110 --> 00:36:21.878
Oh, God. Don't you get it?

482
00:36:21.879 --> 00:36:24.379
You're "the Parzival" now.

483
00:36:24.382 --> 00:36:25.882
You have to have a disguise.

484
00:36:28.152 --> 00:36:29.792
Okay, here.

485
00:36:31.022 --> 00:36:32.722
Clark Kent glasses.

486
00:36:32.723 --> 00:36:35.033
They hide your identity
without changing your look.

487
00:36:43.734 --> 00:36:45.335
I'm not wearing that.

488
00:36:54.879 --> 00:36:57.514
This is great.

489
00:36:57.515 --> 00:36:59.575
The way your inventory
bursts out when you die.

490
00:36:59.584 --> 00:37:01.252
They didn't want
any more blood.

491
00:37:01.253 --> 00:37:02.892
This is right before
the OASIS went live.

492
00:37:02.893 --> 00:37:06.487
Six days prior.
December 2nd, 2025.

493
00:37:06.490 --> 00:37:08.525
Check this out.

494
00:37:08.526 --> 00:37:10.156
You know who that is?

495
00:37:11.762 --> 00:37:13.530
Is that Sorrento?

496
00:37:13.531 --> 00:37:15.500
Sorrento started
as an intern.

497
00:37:15.501 --> 00:37:17.937
He claims he learned
at the feet of the master.

498
00:37:17.938 --> 00:37:20.665
That's how he convinced IOI
to create the Sixers for him,

499
00:37:20.671 --> 00:37:22.239
his Halliday knowledge.

500
00:37:22.240 --> 00:37:24.540
But ask Ogden Morrow?

501
00:37:24.542 --> 00:37:28.712
He says the only thing Sorrento
actually knew about Halliday

502
00:37:28.713 --> 00:37:30.382
was how he liked his coffee.

503
00:37:30.383 --> 00:37:32.881
You could have, like,
different tiers of accounts,

504
00:37:32.883 --> 00:37:34.517
like a gold member.

505
00:37:34.518 --> 00:37:38.188
A person could be
silver, platinum, bronze.

506
00:37:38.189 --> 00:37:40.259
You know, depending on
what they paid.

507
00:37:40.260 --> 00:37:43.128
You know, highest one maybe being
"Water" because "OASIS," right?

508
00:37:43.129 --> 00:37:45.057
Hell of a latte.

509
00:37:45.062 --> 00:37:47.132
Can you fast-forward to the
stuff about Halliday's date?

510
00:37:47.133 --> 00:37:48.971
What? Halliday actually went
on a date?

511
00:37:53.271 --> 00:37:54.738
So, what happened?

512
00:37:54.739 --> 00:37:57.974
Nothing. I invited her over.

513
00:37:57.975 --> 00:38:00.605
Well, did you at least
get her name?

514
00:38:00.611 --> 00:38:04.321
Yeah. Kira, I told you, like the
character in The Dark Crystal.

515
00:38:04.322 --> 00:38:06.145
That's her gamer tag.

516
00:38:08.219 --> 00:38:09.386
- Karen.
- Karen.

517
00:38:09.387 --> 00:38:11.717
Yeah, okay? Karen Underwood.

518
00:38:11.722 --> 00:38:15.325
No, no. Karen Underwood,
as in Ogden Morrow's wife?

519
00:38:15.326 --> 00:38:17.326
Just watch.

520
00:38:17.328 --> 00:38:21.097
So, listen, you and Karen Underwood.
What'd you do?

521
00:38:21.098 --> 00:38:23.566
She wanted to go dancing,

522
00:38:23.567 --> 00:38:25.897
so we watched a movie.

523
00:38:27.138 --> 00:38:28.368
And?

524
00:38:30.308 --> 00:38:32.138
Where's the juice?

525
00:38:32.143 --> 00:38:34.353
Give me some juice!

526
00:38:34.354 --> 00:38:37.745
- There is no juice!
- Oh, God!

527
00:38:37.748 --> 00:38:39.416
Hold the phone.

528
00:38:39.417 --> 00:38:43.517
Halliday went on a date
with Ogden Morrow's wife?

529
00:38:43.521 --> 00:38:46.959
Just once, years before they
were even married, but yeah.

530
00:38:46.960 --> 00:38:49.326
And despite that,
and the fact that she died,

531
00:38:49.327 --> 00:38:52.627
the name "Kira" is only mentioned
once in all of Halliday's Journals.

532
00:38:52.630 --> 00:38:53.960
That's not possible.

533
00:38:53.964 --> 00:38:55.865
It is. Look it up.

534
00:38:55.866 --> 00:38:58.296
What we just saw is the only
time she's ever mentioned.

535
00:38:58.302 --> 00:38:59.802
It makes no sense.

536
00:38:59.804 --> 00:39:02.174
She was an important part
of both their lives.

537
00:39:02.175 --> 00:39:04.113
I'll bet you anything.
All my coin.

538
00:39:05.943 --> 00:39:09.813
Search
"Karen Underwood Morrow."

539
00:39:09.814 --> 00:39:12.984
Kira, I told you, like the
character in The Dark Crystal.

540
00:39:12.985 --> 00:39:15.185
That's her gamer tag.

541
00:39:15.186 --> 00:39:17.886
Halliday purposely removed every
mention of her except for this one.

542
00:39:17.888 --> 00:39:19.518
That's weird. Why?

543
00:39:19.523 --> 00:39:21.533
It's like, it was just
so painful for him

544
00:39:21.534 --> 00:39:24.655
to have to see her face
or hear her name.

545
00:39:24.662 --> 00:39:26.529
Well, he loved her.

546
00:39:26.530 --> 00:39:28.398
He couldn't tell that
to Morrow.

547
00:39:28.399 --> 00:39:30.069
Oh, that's sad. He should
have told her how he felt.

548
00:39:30.070 --> 00:39:31.567
Yeah, well,
he missed his chance.

549
00:39:31.569 --> 00:39:33.699
Look.

550
00:39:33.704 --> 00:39:36.911
I found the clue to the race
in the other scene, but...

551
00:39:36.912 --> 00:39:38.507
I've always felt
that the biggest clue

552
00:39:38.509 --> 00:39:40.379
to the contest
was hidden here.

553
00:39:40.380 --> 00:39:42.148
You're right.

554
00:39:43.214 --> 00:39:45.215
I lose.

555
00:39:45.216 --> 00:39:47.016
Don't sweat it, Curator.

556
00:39:47.017 --> 00:39:49.517
You see, Kira is the Rosebud
at the center of his story.

557
00:39:49.520 --> 00:39:50.720
She's the big mystery.

558
00:39:50.721 --> 00:39:53.091
No, no. A bet is a bet.

559
00:39:54.592 --> 00:39:57.660
Oh, wow. A quarter.
You can keep it.

560
00:39:57.661 --> 00:39:59.801
No. You can keep it.

561
00:40:03.100 --> 00:40:05.470
- You free Thursday?
- Who, me?

562
00:40:06.203 --> 00:40:07.973
No, him.

563
00:40:09.173 --> 00:40:11.013
Oh, my God. Yes, you!

564
00:40:13.277 --> 00:40:15.047
You know The Distracted Globe?

565
00:40:15.048 --> 00:40:17.145
Yeah, the dance club.

566
00:40:19.083 --> 00:40:21.918
Meet me there. 10:00 p.m.

567
00:40:21.919 --> 00:40:24.189
There's something
I wanna show you.

568
00:40:24.955 --> 00:40:26.515
Uh, bye-bye!

569
00:40:27.591 --> 00:40:29.391
Did she just ask me out?

570
00:40:29.393 --> 00:40:31.263
And I was starting
to like her.

571
00:40:31.264 --> 00:40:33.096
All right.

572
00:40:33.097 --> 00:40:34.667
I don't do that.

573
00:40:38.235 --> 00:40:40.295
Z, I can't believe
you told her about Kira.

574
00:40:40.304 --> 00:40:42.872
What? I told you.

575
00:40:42.873 --> 00:40:46.776
Hey, what about this?

576
00:40:46.777 --> 00:40:49.646
No. Have you considered that
Art3mis could be using you?

577
00:40:49.647 --> 00:40:54.117
Hey, dude, she's giving me a clue.
Maybe I'm the one using her.

578
00:40:54.118 --> 00:40:57.718
Should I go more Thriller?

579
00:40:57.721 --> 00:40:59.161
No.

580
00:40:59.890 --> 00:41:00.990
Punk?

581
00:41:00.991 --> 00:41:02.061
No.

582
00:41:04.094 --> 00:41:05.462
Duran Duran.

583
00:41:05.463 --> 00:41:07.297
No.

584
00:41:07.298 --> 00:41:08.468
Does it look like
I'm trying too hard?

585
00:41:08.469 --> 00:41:11.734
Yes! Listen to yourself!

586
00:41:11.735 --> 00:41:14.904
You have a massive cyber crush
on this girl.

587
00:41:14.905 --> 00:41:17.475
She's hacking your heart
to get to your head.

588
00:41:18.976 --> 00:41:20.846
I got it!

589
00:41:21.979 --> 00:41:24.009
- Buckaroo Banzai?
- Yeah!

590
00:41:24.014 --> 00:41:27.283
Really? You're gonna wear the
outfit from your favorite movie?

591
00:41:27.284 --> 00:41:28.651
Don't be that guy.

592
00:41:28.652 --> 00:41:30.687
I am that guy.

593
00:41:30.688 --> 00:41:32.458
Z, you gotta be more careful
about who you meet in the OASIS.

594
00:41:32.459 --> 00:41:35.756
Aech, Art3mis gets me.
She'll get my outfit.

595
00:41:35.759 --> 00:41:38.759
There's just this connection.
I mean, sometimes, we even...

596
00:41:38.762 --> 00:41:40.462
- Finish each other's sentences?
- Yeah!

597
00:41:40.464 --> 00:41:43.366
We have that. Me and you.

598
00:41:43.367 --> 00:41:46.936
Yeah, I know, but that's because
we're best friends, dude.

599
00:41:46.937 --> 00:41:48.867
She could be a dude,
too, dude.

600
00:41:48.873 --> 00:41:50.039
Come on.

601
00:41:50.040 --> 00:41:51.774
I'm serious!

602
00:41:51.775 --> 00:41:54.544
She could actually be
a 300-pound dude

603
00:41:54.545 --> 00:41:57.714
who lives in his mama's
basement in suburban Detroit.

604
00:41:57.715 --> 00:41:59.615
And her name is Chuck.

605
00:42:01.285 --> 00:42:03.885
Think about that.

606
00:42:33.083 --> 00:42:34.493
Whoa, dude,
is that Parzival?

607
00:42:34.494 --> 00:42:36.215
- Parzival!
- Oh, my God, Parzival!

608
00:42:36.220 --> 00:42:39.489
Come here, man.
Hey, can we get a photo?

609
00:42:41.492 --> 00:42:43.832
- Thank you so much!
- Dude, you're my hero!

610
00:42:43.833 --> 00:42:45.157
Hey, Parzival.

611
00:42:47.398 --> 00:42:49.298
Thank you.

612
00:43:03.080 --> 00:43:06.180
Get out of town!
Buckaroo Banzai?

613
00:43:06.183 --> 00:43:08.521
- Huh?
- I like it. I like Buckaroo Banzai.

614
00:43:08.522 --> 00:43:10.189
- Oh, thanks!
- It's great!

615
00:43:10.190 --> 00:43:11.955
- Yeah! You look...
- Oh.

616
00:43:11.956 --> 00:43:13.456
You look awesome!

617
00:43:13.457 --> 00:43:14.657
- Thank you.
- Wow.

618
00:43:16.393 --> 00:43:18.261
A big one, a small one?

619
00:43:18.262 --> 00:43:19.462
A big one!

620
00:43:34.645 --> 00:43:38.314
Get out of here.

621
00:43:38.315 --> 00:43:40.245
- What a freak!
- I thought he was kind of cute.

622
00:43:40.250 --> 00:43:41.788
Have you been here before?

623
00:43:41.789 --> 00:43:43.485
It's cool, right? I mean...

624
00:43:43.487 --> 00:43:45.887
So, what's the plan?

625
00:43:45.889 --> 00:43:48.327
Are you gonna kill their avatars?
Zero them out?

626
00:43:48.328 --> 00:43:50.455
They're both here
at The Distracted Globe.

627
00:43:50.461 --> 00:43:52.929
I can't talk.

628
00:43:52.930 --> 00:43:54.830
The Distracted Globe
was one of the first clubs

629
00:43:54.832 --> 00:43:56.101
Halliday created in the OASIS.

630
00:43:56.102 --> 00:43:57.600
That's common knowledge.

631
00:43:57.601 --> 00:43:59.936
But I double-checked

632
00:43:59.937 --> 00:44:02.407
and it turns out he started building it
right after that moment you showed me.

633
00:44:02.408 --> 00:44:03.666
The date with Kira.

634
00:44:03.674 --> 00:44:05.780
Right, and she was
a serious dancer.

635
00:44:05.781 --> 00:44:07.846
Maybe he thought
he'd take her here,

636
00:44:07.847 --> 00:44:10.675
like on a virtual date.

637
00:44:10.681 --> 00:44:12.581
As if that ever works.

638
00:44:12.583 --> 00:44:14.083
So Halliday built it for her?

639
00:44:14.084 --> 00:44:15.424
But they never made it
past the first date.

640
00:44:15.425 --> 00:44:16.849
So Halliday's the creator...

641
00:44:16.854 --> 00:44:18.187
Who hates his own creation.

642
00:44:18.188 --> 00:44:19.588
And the club
is the thing he hates.

643
00:44:19.590 --> 00:44:21.890
And "A hidden key,
a leap not taken"?

644
00:44:25.295 --> 00:44:26.755
But people jump off it
all night long.

645
00:44:26.764 --> 00:44:28.704
But none of those people
had the Copper Key,

646
00:44:28.705 --> 00:44:32.335
so when we jump off,
maybe it's different. Right?

647
00:44:32.336 --> 00:44:33.396
WADRight.

648
00:44:36.206 --> 00:44:37.676
So we take it together?

649
00:44:37.677 --> 00:44:38.905
Sure.

650
00:44:40.844 --> 00:44:42.984
We're not clanning up
or anything.

651
00:44:42.985 --> 00:44:46.080
Of course not. I don't clan.

652
00:44:47.151 --> 00:44:48.317
Wait...

653
00:44:48.318 --> 00:44:49.688
Whoa!

654
00:44:51.021 --> 00:44:52.761
Ow! Whoa.

655
00:44:57.194 --> 00:45:00.997
I don't think this is it.
No scoreboard, no obstacles.

656
00:45:00.998 --> 00:45:03.698
- Maybe a dance challenge?
- Huh? Whoa!

657
00:45:19.149 --> 00:45:21.149
Old-school!

658
00:45:29.359 --> 00:45:32.328
♪ Well, you can tell
by the way I use my walk

659
00:45:32.329 --> 00:45:34.897
♪ I'm a woman's man
No time to talk

660
00:45:34.898 --> 00:45:37.066
♪ Music loud and women warm

661
00:45:37.067 --> 00:45:39.237
♪ I've been kicked around
since I was born

662
00:45:39.238 --> 00:45:41.866
♪ And now it's all right
I'm okay

663
00:45:41.872 --> 00:45:44.507
♪ And you may look
the other way

664
00:45:44.508 --> 00:45:45.838
You come prepared?

665
00:45:45.843 --> 00:45:47.113
"Prepared"?

666
00:45:50.681 --> 00:45:53.249
What kind of haptics
you rockin'?

667
00:45:53.250 --> 00:45:55.750
You got the gloves and full
visor, or a full body?

668
00:45:55.753 --> 00:45:59.689
♪ Stayin' alive, stayin' alive
Ah, ha, ha, ha

669
00:45:59.690 --> 00:46:01.390
Can you feel this?

670
00:46:01.391 --> 00:46:04.131
♪ Stayin' alive, stayin' alive
Ah, ha, ha, ha

671
00:46:04.132 --> 00:46:06.228
Um, yeah.

672
00:46:06.230 --> 00:46:09.100
I got the X1 haptic bootsuit with
the microfiber crotch inlay.

673
00:46:21.378 --> 00:46:24.348
My, Parzival,
you did come prepared.

674
00:46:27.651 --> 00:46:31.254
So, I've been thinking.

675
00:46:31.255 --> 00:46:33.885
Maybe it'd be cool if we
met up in the real world.

676
00:46:33.891 --> 00:46:35.461
No, you'd be disappointed.

677
00:46:35.462 --> 00:46:38.094
No, I wouldn't. I like you.

678
00:46:38.095 --> 00:46:40.325
You don't even know me.

679
00:46:40.330 --> 00:46:42.170
This isn't
what I really look like.

680
00:46:42.171 --> 00:46:46.166
This isn't my real body,
or my real face.

681
00:46:46.170 --> 00:46:47.904
I don't care.

682
00:46:47.905 --> 00:46:49.465
I wanna know your real name.

683
00:46:49.473 --> 00:46:52.975
Stayin' alive, stayin' alive
Ah, ha, ha, ha

684
00:46:54.178 --> 00:46:56.548
♪ Stayin' alive ♪

685
00:47:02.686 --> 00:47:04.216
- My name's Wade.
- What?

686
00:47:05.689 --> 00:47:07.657
- I said my name's...
- Stop!

687
00:47:07.658 --> 00:47:10.526
Well, Buckaroo blows it.
Shocking.

688
00:47:10.527 --> 00:47:13.157
Are you crazy?
You don't tell anyone who you are.

689
00:47:13.163 --> 00:47:14.669
You can't use your real name.

690
00:47:14.670 --> 00:47:15.925
You're not just anyone.

691
00:47:15.933 --> 00:47:17.633
You don't know me.

692
00:47:17.634 --> 00:47:18.974
You don't know anything about me.
We've never met.

693
00:47:18.975 --> 00:47:20.769
I do know you, Arty.

694
00:47:22.506 --> 00:47:24.066
I'm in love with you.

695
00:47:32.549 --> 00:47:34.949
- Is this part of the challenge?
- No.

696
00:47:34.952 --> 00:47:36.192
It's an ambush.

697
00:47:43.627 --> 00:47:46.357
IOI, always in the way.

698
00:47:46.363 --> 00:47:48.203
Did you hear what I said?
I said I'm in love with you.

699
00:47:48.204 --> 00:47:49.628
No, you're not.

700
00:47:51.168 --> 00:47:52.798
You only know
what I want you to know.

701
00:47:52.803 --> 00:47:54.713
You only see
what I want you to see.

702
00:47:57.574 --> 00:47:59.444
That's what
you're in love with.

703
00:48:13.257 --> 00:48:14.457
Watch out!

704
00:48:24.668 --> 00:48:26.138
Pull.

705
00:48:38.715 --> 00:48:41.915
Head back! Z!
Your armor is running low.

706
00:48:41.919 --> 00:48:43.119
I just bought this.

707
00:48:51.128 --> 00:48:52.428
Zemeckis Cube.

708
00:48:52.429 --> 00:48:54.329
Turns everything
back in time 60 seconds.

709
00:48:58.902 --> 00:49:00.972
And you waited
until now to use it?

710
00:49:09.046 --> 00:49:11.206
Wow, you were amazing.

711
00:49:14.318 --> 00:49:16.548
This isn't a game, Z.

712
00:49:17.821 --> 00:49:19.789
I'm doing this to stop IOI.

713
00:49:19.790 --> 00:49:22.290
I'm talking about
real-world consequences.

714
00:49:22.292 --> 00:49:23.892
People suffering.

715
00:49:23.894 --> 00:49:25.764
- Actual life-and-death stuff.
- I know. I know...

716
00:49:25.765 --> 00:49:30.666
No, you don't know!
My dad died in a loyalty center.

717
00:49:30.667 --> 00:49:33.836
- He borrowed gear.
- He built up debt.

718
00:49:33.837 --> 00:49:37.337
He moved in with the promise of
working it off, but he never did.

719
00:49:37.341 --> 00:49:39.241
IOI just raised
his living expenses,

720
00:49:39.242 --> 00:49:40.812
then he got sick, and he
couldn't afford to get out.

721
00:49:40.813 --> 00:49:43.311
And then he died!

722
00:49:43.313 --> 00:49:44.682
I'm so sorry, I didn't...

723
00:49:44.683 --> 00:49:46.781
No, you don't live
in the real world, Z.

724
00:49:46.783 --> 00:49:49.852
From what you've told me,
I don't think you ever have.

725
00:49:49.853 --> 00:49:53.456
You live inside this...
This illusion,

726
00:49:53.457 --> 00:49:55.527
and I can't afford
to let you distract me.

727
00:50:08.138 --> 00:50:10.468
How the hell
did they get away?

728
00:50:10.474 --> 00:50:12.780
Do you want the long version?
Your guys suck.

729
00:50:12.781 --> 00:50:14.476
They failed
to kill his avatar,

730
00:50:14.478 --> 00:50:16.708
which, if we're offering
constructive criticism,

731
00:50:16.713 --> 00:50:19.551
was a lame idea and only
would've slowed him down.

732
00:50:19.552 --> 00:50:23.889
Whereas my plan, which was cool
because I rock, actually worked.

733
00:50:23.890 --> 00:50:25.654
He's still on the board.

734
00:50:25.655 --> 00:50:29.185
I know that, Nolan.
But he won't be for long.

735
00:50:29.192 --> 00:50:31.162
I did a search
for all the Wades

736
00:50:31.163 --> 00:50:33.361
who had recently bought
an X1 bootsuit,

737
00:50:33.363 --> 00:50:36.573
cross-referenced that with
public records, and voila,

738
00:50:36.574 --> 00:50:40.636
which is French for...
"And then I found out."

739
00:50:41.204 --> 00:50:42.972
Ready?

740
00:50:42.973 --> 00:50:47.283
The real-world identity
of Parzival is Wade Watts.

741
00:50:48.011 --> 00:50:49.611
Voila.

742
00:50:51.248 --> 00:50:54.148
Are you loyal, Ms. Zandor?

743
00:50:54.151 --> 00:50:55.918
You really want me
to answer that?

744
00:50:55.919 --> 00:50:57.489
Well, when you're at war,

745
00:50:57.490 --> 00:51:00.517
you need people
who are loyal to a fault.

746
00:51:00.524 --> 00:51:02.393
People you can count on
to get things done.

747
00:51:02.394 --> 00:51:05.061
I just get people arrested
for not paying their bills.

748
00:51:05.062 --> 00:51:08.000
Yeah, 'cause there are some problems
that require a physical solution,

749
00:51:08.001 --> 00:51:10.568
but there are other times,
particularly at war,

750
00:51:10.569 --> 00:51:12.267
when you need
a different set of rules.

751
00:51:12.269 --> 00:51:14.099
- The rules of war.
- Exactly.

752
00:51:14.104 --> 00:51:16.710
It's too bad my division doesn't
operate inside the OASIS.

753
00:51:16.711 --> 00:51:19.606
Yeah, but if this war
remains in the OASIS,

754
00:51:19.609 --> 00:51:22.009
then you can't do anything.

755
00:51:22.012 --> 00:51:24.947
So, this is one of those conversations
that we're not really having.

756
00:51:24.948 --> 00:51:26.718
Well, we've had these kind
of conversations before,

757
00:51:26.719 --> 00:51:28.446
and look where you are now.

758
00:51:28.452 --> 00:51:30.752
You got a seat on the board,
head of your own division,

759
00:51:30.754 --> 00:51:34.423
a division that will cease to exist if
the wrong person wins this contest.

760
00:51:34.424 --> 00:51:37.760
F'Nale, a game decides
our fate.

761
00:51:37.761 --> 00:51:41.601
The only question is, how far
are we willing to go to win it?

762
00:51:43.733 --> 00:51:45.843
Tell me what you need, Nolan.

763
00:53:04.147 --> 00:53:05.717
Whoa.

764
00:53:09.486 --> 00:53:11.146
Where am I?

765
00:53:11.154 --> 00:53:13.464
IOI Plaza.
You're a hologram in the real world.

766
00:53:14.324 --> 00:53:15.991
That's a really cool rig.

767
00:53:15.992 --> 00:53:20.029
Thank you.
It's a brand-new Habashaw, OIR 9400.

768
00:53:20.030 --> 00:53:22.030
It looks like
a giant hamster ball.

769
00:53:22.032 --> 00:53:26.802
You know, if you came to work
at IOI, you'd get one of these.

770
00:53:26.803 --> 00:53:28.737
I don't clan up.

771
00:53:28.738 --> 00:53:30.968
You'd also get your own
penthouse apartment in Columbus

772
00:53:30.974 --> 00:53:33.244
with the
highest-speed connection.

773
00:53:33.245 --> 00:53:38.647
In the OASIS, you'd get unlimited weapons,
magic items, ships.

774
00:53:38.648 --> 00:53:40.518
You want the ship
from Defender?

775
00:53:40.519 --> 00:53:43.247
You know, the kind that can
just jump into hyperspace?

776
00:53:43.253 --> 00:53:45.163
You want
the Millennium Falcon?

777
00:53:46.056 --> 00:53:47.516
You have that?

778
00:53:47.524 --> 00:53:50.362
Anything you need
to help you find that egg,

779
00:53:50.363 --> 00:53:51.730
and then there's the salary.

780
00:53:52.829 --> 00:53:54.929
Four million a year.

781
00:53:54.931 --> 00:53:58.541
And if you do happen to find that
Easter egg, there's a bonus.

782
00:53:58.542 --> 00:54:00.835
Twenty-five million dollars.

783
00:54:06.209 --> 00:54:09.778
I can see you're using
emotion-suppressing software right now,

784
00:54:09.779 --> 00:54:12.679
and why wouldn't you?
It's smart, not to show your hand.

785
00:54:18.121 --> 00:54:21.861
It is a lot of money.
I could really use it.

786
00:54:26.796 --> 00:54:29.196
But I don't think you and I
would have the same plans.

787
00:54:29.199 --> 00:54:32.239
Well, I don't know about that.
What, for the OASIS?

788
00:54:32.240 --> 00:54:35.435
I guess if you're not
a John Hughes fan...

789
00:54:36.539 --> 00:54:38.274
Of course I am.

790
00:54:38.275 --> 00:54:40.905
Because the first thing
that I would do

791
00:54:40.910 --> 00:54:44.647
is convert all the schools
on Ludus to replicas

792
00:54:44.648 --> 00:54:47.816
from The Breakfast Club
and Ferris Bueller.

793
00:54:47.817 --> 00:54:50.986
No way. That's a great idea.

794
00:54:50.987 --> 00:54:53.455
Which school,
Ridgemont or Faber?

795
00:54:53.456 --> 00:54:56.556
Fast Times at Ridgemont High,
not John Hughes.

796
00:54:56.559 --> 00:54:59.795
It's a trap. Faber College
from Animal House.

797
00:54:59.796 --> 00:55:01.426
John Hughes didn't direct

798
00:55:01.431 --> 00:55:04.431
Fast Times at Ridgemont High
or Animal House.

799
00:55:04.434 --> 00:55:07.773
Ferris Bueller and The Breakfast Club,
they went to Shermer High School,

800
00:55:07.774 --> 00:55:11.310
which is in Shermer, Illinois.
I know what you think.

801
00:55:11.311 --> 00:55:13.008
You think
I'm a corporate asshole,

802
00:55:13.009 --> 00:55:16.409
that I don't appreciate
pop culture, but...

803
00:55:16.413 --> 00:55:19.523
Man, that's not true.
You know, when I wanna blow off steam...

804
00:55:19.524 --> 00:55:23.485
Drink Tab, plRobotron,
listen to Duran Duran.

805
00:55:23.486 --> 00:55:25.086
I crack open a Tab.

806
00:55:25.088 --> 00:55:27.488
I put on some Duran Duran.
I play Robotron.

807
00:55:27.490 --> 00:55:29.625
That's why I love the OASIS.

808
00:55:29.626 --> 00:55:32.956
'Cause it's just full
of all these things, man,

809
00:55:32.962 --> 00:55:34.502
that people love. You know?

810
00:55:42.305 --> 00:55:44.805
I'm a businessman. I get it.

811
00:55:44.808 --> 00:55:47.608
But I gotta do my job.

812
00:55:47.610 --> 00:55:53.349
But I didn't ask you here just
to help us find the egg, Parzival.

813
00:55:53.350 --> 00:55:57.190
I asked you here
for what comes after.

814
00:55:58.355 --> 00:56:00.055
What would Halliday say?

815
00:56:01.057 --> 00:56:03.787
James Halliday is dead.

816
00:56:05.028 --> 00:56:09.028
Yeah. He is.

817
00:56:09.032 --> 00:56:13.969
All that's left of him is this contest.
And you know what?

818
00:56:13.970 --> 00:56:16.340
It just seems like he
wouldn't want you winning it.

819
00:56:16.341 --> 00:56:18.339
A fanboy knows a hater,

820
00:56:18.341 --> 00:56:20.411
and I know you've got a whole
department of oologists in your ear.

821
00:56:20.412 --> 00:56:22.680
So, if you wanna know
what I really think...

822
00:56:22.681 --> 00:56:24.209
I think you're full of shit.

823
00:56:29.519 --> 00:56:31.186
Here's my offer.

824
00:56:31.187 --> 00:56:32.687
Your board of directors,
you got them in the other ear?

825
00:56:32.689 --> 00:56:34.619
Why don't you tell 'em this.

826
00:56:35.759 --> 00:56:38.559
If they dump you,
I'll consider it.

827
00:56:38.561 --> 00:56:40.661
I might say something
off the record.

828
00:56:41.664 --> 00:56:43.699
I had to make the offer.

829
00:56:43.700 --> 00:56:46.700
The board expected it, but I was
really hoping you'd say no.

830
00:56:46.703 --> 00:56:50.113
Because if anyone's gonna win
this competition, it's me.

831
00:56:50.114 --> 00:56:52.174
My avatar gets the egg

832
00:56:52.175 --> 00:56:55.544
'cause I'm the only one here with
the balls to run this place.

833
00:56:55.545 --> 00:56:58.045
Wow, you really
switched gears there.

834
00:56:58.047 --> 00:57:01.116
From fairly reasonable
to maniacal overlord.

835
00:57:01.117 --> 00:57:04.117
You should be grateful, Wade.

836
00:57:04.120 --> 00:57:07.556
You won't be around
to endure my maniacal reign.

837
00:57:07.557 --> 00:57:09.357
Yeah, that's right.
I know who you are.

838
00:57:09.359 --> 00:57:14.596
Wade Owen Watts,
born August 12, 2027.

839
00:57:14.597 --> 00:57:18.597
I also know where you are.
Unit 56K, Columbus stacks.

840
00:57:18.601 --> 00:57:21.370
You were last seen entering
your trailer three days ago.

841
00:57:21.371 --> 00:57:22.805
You haven't left since.

842
00:57:22.806 --> 00:57:24.136
What are you doing?
You can't...

843
00:57:24.140 --> 00:57:25.740
With all that's going on
in the world,

844
00:57:25.742 --> 00:57:27.112
do you really think that
anyone's gonna give a damn

845
00:57:27.113 --> 00:57:28.644
about an explosion

846
00:57:28.645 --> 00:57:31.205
in some ghetto trash
rat warren in Columbus?

847
00:57:31.214 --> 00:57:33.454
Sorrento, don't do this.
I'm not even there!

848
00:57:33.455 --> 00:57:35.350
Not for long.

849
00:57:38.988 --> 00:57:41.218
Call Alice.

850
00:57:41.224 --> 00:57:42.964
Dial Alice.

851
00:58:09.419 --> 00:58:11.319
Pick up! Pick up! Alice!

852
00:58:16.359 --> 00:58:18.829
This bootsuit's pretty awesome.
Thanks for that.

853
00:58:18.830 --> 00:58:20.928
Rick! Rick, the place
is gonna blow!

854
00:58:20.930 --> 00:58:22.430
Rick, is that Wade?

855
00:58:22.432 --> 00:58:24.632
- Put Alice on!
- Let me talk to him.

856
00:58:24.634 --> 00:58:26.644
Don't call here anymore,
you got me?

857
00:58:28.137 --> 00:58:30.937
I don't wanna hear your voice
ever again.

858
00:59:07.911 --> 00:59:12.314
Contact Aech, Daito,
Sho, and Art3mis.

859
00:59:12.315 --> 00:59:14.515
IOI came for me
in the real world.

860
00:59:14.517 --> 00:59:17.317
They gotta be coming after you,
so wherever you are...

861
00:59:43.379 --> 00:59:45.414
Sorry about the blindfold.

862
00:59:45.415 --> 00:59:47.615
My guys are a little paranoid.

863
00:59:48.418 --> 00:59:50.618
Say that again.

864
00:59:50.620 --> 00:59:53.020
My guys are a little paranoid.

865
00:59:54.090 --> 00:59:55.590
Art3mis?

866
00:59:57.093 --> 01:00:01.163
My real name is Samantha,
but yeah, I'm Art3mis.

867
01:00:03.032 --> 01:00:05.772
Showers are that way,
clean clothes, too.

868
01:00:09.038 --> 01:00:13.108
Welcome to the rebellion,
Wade.

869
01:00:24.253 --> 01:00:29.758
That's IOI.
So the stacks are over there?

870
01:00:29.759 --> 01:00:32.629
We've been living this close
to each other the whole time?

871
01:00:34.063 --> 01:00:36.231
Next door,

872
01:00:36.232 --> 01:00:40.342
around the world,
it's... it's all the same in the OASIS.

873
01:00:42.772 --> 01:00:45.172
For the record,

874
01:00:45.174 --> 01:00:46.675
um...

875
01:00:46.676 --> 01:00:50.676
I'm not disappointed.

876
01:00:50.680 --> 01:00:53.780
You said I... I would be
disappointed when I met you, but...

877
01:00:53.783 --> 01:00:57.019
I'm not.

878
01:00:57.020 --> 01:00:59.860
I've lived with it my whole life.
You don't have to pretend.

879
01:01:14.370 --> 01:01:17.170
You have a birthmark, so what?

880
01:01:18.041 --> 01:01:19.781
Why would that scare me?

881
01:01:26.983 --> 01:01:29.618
Z, if I hurt you,
I'm... I'm sorry.

882
01:01:29.619 --> 01:01:31.819
No, it's...

883
01:01:31.821 --> 01:01:35.121
Wait, did... did you
just call me "Z"?

884
01:01:35.124 --> 01:01:37.164
- Oh, my God. Did I?
- I think you did.

885
01:01:37.165 --> 01:01:39.027
Wade, I'm sorry.

886
01:01:39.028 --> 01:01:41.358
Yeah, Wade, Z.

887
01:01:41.364 --> 01:01:44.674
You can call me whatever you want.
And I'll call you Sam.

888
01:01:44.675 --> 01:01:45.737
No.

889
01:01:46.803 --> 01:01:48.303
Uh, Samantha?

890
01:01:48.304 --> 01:01:50.574
Okay. Cool.

891
01:01:57.847 --> 01:01:59.617
Wow.

892
01:02:00.416 --> 01:02:02.546
It's so much slower here.

893
01:02:03.886 --> 01:02:07.256
I mean, the wind,
the people...

894
01:02:09.092 --> 01:02:10.962
Everything.

895
01:02:16.165 --> 01:02:18.595
We forget what it's like
to be outside.

896
01:02:18.601 --> 01:02:19.671
Yeah.

897
01:02:22.939 --> 01:02:26.408
- Uh...
- Oh, shit!

898
01:02:26.409 --> 01:02:28.077
- I just figured it out.
- Figured what out?

899
01:02:28.078 --> 01:02:29.558
The second clue.
I know what it means.

900
01:02:35.852 --> 01:02:37.922
We've been thinking about it
too literally.

901
01:02:37.923 --> 01:02:39.454
"The leap not taken,"

902
01:02:39.455 --> 01:02:41.685
the leap Halliday didn't take,
is with Kira.

903
01:02:41.691 --> 01:02:45.531
Yeah, but... I mean, he blamed her
for breaking up him and Morrow.

904
01:02:45.532 --> 01:02:48.458
No. Halliday was madly
in love with her.

905
01:02:48.464 --> 01:02:50.904
He had a chance with Kira. He had
a chance to kiss her, but...

906
01:02:50.905 --> 01:02:52.240
He didn't take the leap.

907
01:02:52.241 --> 01:02:55.965
Right. So that's where
we go next.

908
01:02:55.972 --> 01:02:57.542
The place where the leap
wasn't taken.

909
01:02:57.543 --> 01:02:59.207
Where the date was.

910
01:02:59.208 --> 01:03:01.376
At the movies!

911
01:03:01.377 --> 01:03:03.145
Hey, Curator.

912
01:03:03.146 --> 01:03:05.146
We figured out the second clue.
The challenge is here.

913
01:03:05.148 --> 01:03:07.218
Halliday kept track of every
movie he ever watched,

914
01:03:07.219 --> 01:03:10.285
the week and the year he watched it,
and how many times.

915
01:03:10.286 --> 01:03:15.056
Curator, can we see
November 23 to 27, 2025?

916
01:03:15.057 --> 01:03:16.887
That's the week
he went on the date with Kira.

917
01:03:21.464 --> 01:03:25.103
Okay, so our options for that
week are The Fly remake.

918
01:03:25.104 --> 01:03:27.241
Great flick,
terrible date movie.

919
01:03:27.242 --> 01:03:30.736
Say Anything...
That would make sense.

920
01:03:30.740 --> 01:03:35.180
We gotta remember the clue.
"A creator who hates his own creation."

921
01:03:39.782 --> 01:03:41.750
The Shining!

922
01:03:41.751 --> 01:03:44.021
It's Halliday's
11th favorite horror film,

923
01:03:44.022 --> 01:03:46.420
and it's based on the best-selling
book by Stephen King,

924
01:03:46.422 --> 01:03:48.022
who hated the movie!

925
01:03:48.024 --> 01:03:50.125
Hey! No side chitchat.

926
01:03:50.126 --> 01:03:51.486
I think we found it.

927
01:03:55.198 --> 01:03:57.928
Are you absolutely sure
you want to go here?

928
01:03:57.934 --> 01:03:59.801
Absolutely positive.

929
01:03:59.802 --> 01:04:02.637
Let's hope
you have the belly for it.

930
01:04:45.581 --> 01:04:46.751
Look.

931
01:04:48.184 --> 01:04:50.352
Ticking clock.

932
01:04:50.353 --> 01:04:53.163
Okay, so I'm estimating about

933
01:04:54.190 --> 01:04:56.224
five minutes to find the key.

934
01:04:56.225 --> 01:04:57.855
Yeah, there are so many keys
The Shining, though.

935
01:04:57.860 --> 01:05:00.695
Where do we start?

936
01:05:00.696 --> 01:05:04.096
I've never seen The Shining.
Is it really scary?

937
01:05:04.100 --> 01:05:08.036
Uh, I had to watch it
through my fingers.

938
01:05:08.037 --> 01:05:11.006
Okay, so we got the key
from room 237,

939
01:05:11.007 --> 01:05:12.907
the keys to the Snowcat,

940
01:05:12.909 --> 01:05:14.739
or the keys they give Jack
at the beginning of the movie.

941
01:05:14.744 --> 01:05:16.550
Well,
if it's "the leap not taken,"

942
01:05:16.551 --> 01:05:18.005
maybe the key
isn't a key at all.

943
01:05:18.014 --> 01:05:19.084
I know
where the Snowcat keys are!

944
01:05:19.085 --> 01:05:20.281
I say we split up.

945
01:05:20.283 --> 01:05:21.950
We get all the keys

946
01:05:21.951 --> 01:05:23.911
and then we meet back
at the Torrances' apartment.

947
01:05:27.423 --> 01:05:29.133
Hello, Danny.

948
01:05:30.293 --> 01:05:32.093
Come play with us.

949
01:05:32.094 --> 01:05:35.364
Little girls, y'all know
how to get out of here?

950
01:05:40.303 --> 01:05:41.469
Wait, wait!

951
01:05:41.470 --> 01:05:43.605
Wait, where's Aech?

952
01:05:43.606 --> 01:05:44.936
Wait!

953
01:05:45.975 --> 01:05:47.035
Aech!

954
01:05:47.777 --> 01:05:48.877
No, no, no, no!

955
01:06:07.063 --> 01:06:08.733
Ahh!

956
01:06:13.402 --> 01:06:15.042
Ahh!

957
01:06:48.504 --> 01:06:51.373
Oh, uh, hi, naked lady.
I'm sorry.

958
01:06:51.374 --> 01:06:53.480
I didn't mean to interrupt,
uh, your bath time.

959
01:06:53.481 --> 01:06:55.536
Uh, I know self-care
can be important.

960
01:06:55.544 --> 01:06:58.714
Uh, but can you do me a favor and
tell me, where are all the exits?

961
01:07:02.284 --> 01:07:03.852
Huh. Whoa.

962
01:07:03.853 --> 01:07:06.221
Okay, am I being punked?

963
01:07:06.222 --> 01:07:08.622
'Cause you're likin' me
a little way too much.

964
01:07:10.126 --> 01:07:12.286
All right, you know what?
I'ma go with it.

965
01:07:25.808 --> 01:07:26.908
Ahh!

966
01:08:04.180 --> 01:08:05.580
Time's running out.

967
01:08:05.581 --> 01:08:07.715
Yo, Z, is Art3mis
pissed at me?

968
01:08:07.716 --> 01:08:10.116
Dude, I'm pissed at you.
You've never seen The Shining, have you?

969
01:08:10.119 --> 01:08:11.519
You know I hate scary movies!

970
01:08:11.520 --> 01:08:12.687
We got the key.

971
01:08:12.688 --> 01:08:14.088
Sweet! To room 237!

972
01:08:14.090 --> 01:08:16.630
We ain't got no business
goin' to room 237!

973
01:08:16.631 --> 01:08:18.425
We should stay out!

974
01:08:18.427 --> 01:08:20.057
Plus, there was this crazy,
naked zombie lady in there.

975
01:08:20.062 --> 01:08:21.762
There are no zombies
The Shining.

976
01:08:21.764 --> 01:08:23.732
Well, maybe it's not supposed
to be like the movie.

977
01:08:23.733 --> 01:08:25.432
Kira is the key.
You're the one who said it.

978
01:08:25.434 --> 01:08:27.644
Hey, y'all.
I saw a picture of Kira!

979
01:08:27.645 --> 01:08:29.766
Huh?

980
01:08:32.241 --> 01:08:33.341
Where?

981
01:08:40.282 --> 01:08:44.419
It's Kira.
"Escape your past."

982
01:08:44.420 --> 01:08:47.620
"The leap not taken."

983
01:08:47.623 --> 01:08:49.633
Halliday's greatest fear
wasn't The Shining

984
01:08:49.634 --> 01:08:52.085
or any book or movie.

985
01:08:52.094 --> 01:08:55.663
His biggest fear
was kissing a girl.

986
01:08:55.664 --> 01:08:59.234
That's the leap
he couldn't take.

987
01:09:06.175 --> 01:09:07.875
The ballroom.

988
01:09:22.458 --> 01:09:24.588
Aech, come on.

989
01:09:28.130 --> 01:09:30.170
Zombies. Told you.

990
01:09:31.534 --> 01:09:32.844
That's her.

991
01:09:33.869 --> 01:09:34.869
That's Kira.

992
01:09:38.374 --> 01:09:40.375
None of this
is in The Shining.

993
01:09:40.376 --> 01:09:42.646
Z, look. That's the zombie-circle
level in Mayhem Mansion,

994
01:09:42.647 --> 01:09:44.275
one of Halliday's first games.

995
01:09:44.280 --> 01:09:46.120
The whole Shining trivia
is just a diversion.

996
01:09:47.316 --> 01:09:48.946
One minute left.

997
01:09:50.352 --> 01:09:51.692
How do we get to her?

998
01:09:51.693 --> 01:09:52.854
Take the leap.

999
01:09:52.855 --> 01:09:53.915
Wait!

1000
01:09:55.291 --> 01:09:56.431
Whoa!

1001
01:10:02.231 --> 01:10:04.999
Okay, Mr. Dead Guy.
Cool if I lead?

1002
01:10:52.615 --> 01:10:54.915
Care to dance?

1003
01:10:54.917 --> 01:10:58.447
Do you know how long I've
been waiting for you to ask?

1004
01:11:04.260 --> 01:11:06.860
Well, well, well.

1005
01:11:06.862 --> 01:11:11.302
So you found my Jade Key.

1006
01:11:13.736 --> 01:11:15.696
Imagine that.

1007
01:11:20.643 --> 01:11:22.283
Thank you.

1008
01:11:26.982 --> 01:11:29.122
- Kira was a very beautiful...
- Go on.

1009
01:11:58.113 --> 01:12:01.182
One of our oologists saw them
enter the media library.

1010
01:12:01.183 --> 01:12:02.850
She cracked the clue.

1011
01:12:02.851 --> 01:12:06.654
Now, we just have to win
The Shining challenge.

1012
01:12:08.991 --> 01:12:11.791
Get her off me!
Get her off me!

1013
01:12:21.203 --> 01:12:25.773
Mr. Sorrento, I really think
you need to see this.

1014
01:12:27.843 --> 01:12:29.713
Now Parzival's
got the Jade Key.

1015
01:12:40.055 --> 01:12:42.455
He's alive.

1016
01:12:42.458 --> 01:12:45.388
I know. I'll get back to you.

1017
01:12:45.394 --> 01:12:47.464
I got what you're looking for.

1018
01:12:51.333 --> 01:12:55.603
Freeze. This guy.
The one with the lame tattoo.

1019
01:12:59.842 --> 01:13:03.082
Run him through our database,
every IOI drone in Columbus.

1020
01:13:03.083 --> 01:13:04.578
Find him.

1021
01:13:31.440 --> 01:13:33.174
Groceries are here.

1022
01:13:33.175 --> 01:13:34.675
All right. Gluten-O's...

1023
01:13:34.676 --> 01:13:35.906
"If you know
the answer ultimate,

1024
01:13:35.911 --> 01:13:38.179
"divide it
by the number magic,

1025
01:13:38.180 --> 01:13:41.018
"and what you need, want, and desire
will be found in the fortress tragic."

1026
01:13:41.019 --> 01:13:43.116
"Tragic," that's gotta be
Halliday referring to himself.

1027
01:13:43.118 --> 01:13:44.218
Why?

1028
01:13:44.219 --> 01:13:46.019
Because he was lonely.

1029
01:13:46.021 --> 01:13:47.921
He had no one to spend his
life with towards the end.

1030
01:13:47.923 --> 01:13:50.024
Yeah, that's true.

1031
01:13:50.025 --> 01:13:51.955
The contest has gotta be somehow
about connecting with someone.

1032
01:13:51.960 --> 01:13:53.528
Anyone.

1033
01:13:53.529 --> 01:13:55.029
He wants the person
who cares for the OASIS

1034
01:13:55.030 --> 01:13:56.730
to be connected
with the world.

1035
01:13:56.732 --> 01:13:59.272
That's what I think
he's trying to tell us.

1036
01:14:05.207 --> 01:14:06.877
Wade.

1037
01:14:08.877 --> 01:14:11.207
You understand Halliday.

1038
01:14:11.213 --> 01:14:14.916
You know him
better than anyone.

1039
01:14:14.917 --> 01:14:17.917
It's exactly
why I think you'll win.

1040
01:14:17.920 --> 01:14:21.790
Really? You really think
I'm gonna win?

1041
01:14:25.661 --> 01:14:27.461
Do not move!

1042
01:14:32.835 --> 01:14:34.335
Target identified!

1043
01:14:35.337 --> 01:14:36.967
Freeze! Don't move!

1044
01:14:43.779 --> 01:14:46.417
- This leads right to the alley.
- You first.

1045
01:14:46.418 --> 01:14:48.145
I'm right behind you. Go now!

1046
01:14:49.685 --> 01:14:51.285
Come on!

1047
01:14:51.286 --> 01:14:53.786
- Wade, the OASIS needs you.
- What?

1048
01:14:53.789 --> 01:14:55.089
- I'm gonna delay them.
- Wait!

1049
01:14:55.090 --> 01:14:57.525
No, no, no, wait! No, no, no!

1050
01:14:57.526 --> 01:14:59.756
You'll forgive me
for this, I promise.

1051
01:15:08.937 --> 01:15:10.567
Freeze, freeze, freeze!

1052
01:15:11.540 --> 01:15:12.610
Don't move!

1053
01:15:17.846 --> 01:15:20.546
Samantha Evelyn Cook.

1054
01:15:20.549 --> 01:15:24.218
IOI has purchased and consolidated
all of your outstanding debt,

1055
01:15:24.219 --> 01:15:27.488
currently in excess
of 23,000 credits.

1056
01:15:27.489 --> 01:15:30.358
You will be remanded to the
nearest IOI loyalty center

1057
01:15:30.359 --> 01:15:31.859
until your debt
is paid in full,

1058
01:15:31.860 --> 01:15:34.660
including any interest,
processing,

1059
01:15:34.663 --> 01:15:37.331
or late fees
you incur henceforth.

1060
01:15:37.332 --> 01:15:39.892
- Does anybody have eyes?
- Check down the next street!

1061
01:15:52.347 --> 01:15:54.547
- "First to the key."
- "First to the egg."

1062
01:15:54.550 --> 01:15:56.850
Wait, what?

1063
01:15:56.852 --> 01:16:00.221
"Never trust someone you meet
in the OASIS."

1064
01:16:00.222 --> 01:16:02.860
"She might be a 300-pound dude
named Chuck..."

1065
01:16:02.861 --> 01:16:06.128
"Who lives in his mama's
basement in suburban Detroit."

1066
01:16:08.430 --> 01:16:10.364
Aech!

1067
01:16:10.365 --> 01:16:13.935
Helen. My dad called me "H."
It kinda stuck. Let's go!

1068
01:16:23.745 --> 01:16:25.975
That thing's IDing my van.

1069
01:16:40.762 --> 01:16:42.832
Come on. They've spotted us.

1070
01:16:43.599 --> 01:16:45.199
Daito.

1071
01:16:45.200 --> 01:16:48.038
My real name is Toshiro.
Samantha got us a message.

1072
01:16:48.039 --> 01:16:49.866
She told us to meet you here.

1073
01:16:49.871 --> 01:16:51.271
Samantha,
they took her to the...

1074
01:16:51.273 --> 01:16:53.307
The loyalty center, I know.

1075
01:16:53.308 --> 01:16:56.877
Look, in other awesome news,
the Sixers found the third challenge.

1076
01:16:56.878 --> 01:16:58.778
- What?
- Just come on, get in!

1077
01:16:58.780 --> 01:16:59.980
All right. Let's go.

1078
01:16:59.982 --> 01:17:02.182
Hurry up.
Go, go, go. All right.

1079
01:17:13.895 --> 01:17:16.395
How did IOI find
the third challenge so fast?

1080
01:17:16.398 --> 01:17:18.498
IOI cracked the first
three lines of the clue,

1081
01:17:18.500 --> 01:17:20.167
so they knew it was sector 14

1082
01:17:20.168 --> 01:17:21.768
but they couldn't figure out
"the fortress tragic."

1083
01:17:21.770 --> 01:17:24.170
So they sent every guide
they had into that sector

1084
01:17:24.172 --> 01:17:26.142
until they found
the right fortress.

1085
01:17:27.175 --> 01:17:28.635
Sho?

1086
01:17:28.644 --> 01:17:30.954
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
I'm 11, so what?

1087
01:17:30.955 --> 01:17:32.976
His real name is Xo.

1088
01:17:32.981 --> 01:17:35.750
But everyone else calls me Sho,
no big deal.

1089
01:17:35.751 --> 01:17:38.519
No. It is a big deal.

1090
01:17:38.520 --> 01:17:42.089
Sho, you're the world's most
badass 11-year-old ever.

1091
01:17:42.090 --> 01:17:43.157
He knows.

1092
01:17:43.158 --> 01:17:45.358
Shut up! Let him tell me.

1093
01:17:45.360 --> 01:17:46.500
Aech!

1094
01:17:49.965 --> 01:17:51.665
We have to go save Samantha.

1095
01:17:51.667 --> 01:17:54.035
Well, we can't just
go through the doors of IOI.

1096
01:17:54.036 --> 01:17:56.266
Look, I've been thinkin' about it.
I got a better plan.

1097
01:17:56.271 --> 01:17:58.271
You saw Sorrento's rig, right?

1098
01:17:58.273 --> 01:18:00.374
Yeah.

1099
01:18:00.375 --> 01:18:02.805
Let's go after the man himself and
make him give Art3mis back to us.

1100
01:18:02.811 --> 01:18:04.711
But first,
I have to know exactly,

1101
01:18:04.713 --> 01:18:06.723
how much about Sorrento's rig
do you remember?

1102
01:18:08.116 --> 01:18:10.416
Kind of everything.

1103
01:18:24.132 --> 01:18:28.042
Maintenance,
report to loyalty pod 31-B.

1104
01:18:32.074 --> 01:18:36.714
Security, please report
to section 97 for escort.

1105
01:18:57.432 --> 01:19:00.302
Hey! Newbie, get to work.

1106
01:19:02.437 --> 01:19:03.567
Get to work.

1107
01:19:09.878 --> 01:19:13.008
Work violation. Work violation.

1108
01:19:14.750 --> 01:19:17.850
Lay those charges
every six feet.

1109
01:19:22.858 --> 01:19:25.028
Keep it moving!

1110
01:19:26.294 --> 01:19:27.364
Hey, you!

1111
01:19:29.464 --> 01:19:31.298
Those are explosives!

1112
01:19:33.034 --> 01:19:36.244
IOI will not reimburse
any lost coin if you zero out.

1113
01:19:36.245 --> 01:19:38.038
Keep it moving!

1114
01:19:42.744 --> 01:19:45.784
So what is this challenge,
some sort of video game thing?

1115
01:19:45.785 --> 01:19:47.881
An Atari 2600, sir.

1116
01:19:47.883 --> 01:19:51.493
And every game ever made for it,
thousands of possibilities.

1117
01:19:52.254 --> 01:19:53.621
Come up!

1118
01:19:58.093 --> 01:19:59.560
Halliday,

1119
01:19:59.561 --> 01:20:01.499
this is how
you plan to resolve

1120
01:20:01.500 --> 01:20:04.926
the fate of the world's most
important economic resource?

1121
01:20:04.933 --> 01:20:06.903
- Call me when you're close.
- Yes, sir.

1122
01:20:06.904 --> 01:20:08.502
Go, go! No! Ahh!

1123
01:20:10.772 --> 01:20:13.941
One minute into Centipede,
the ice broke.

1124
01:20:13.942 --> 01:20:16.010
It has to be Joust!

1125
01:20:16.011 --> 01:20:18.949
Halliday still holds the world record
on the 2600 port of that game.

1126
01:20:18.950 --> 01:20:20.947
Maybe we just need
to beat his high score.

1127
01:20:20.949 --> 01:20:23.249
Pitfall! One of the only 2600
games that still hasn't ended.

1128
01:20:23.251 --> 01:20:24.691
And how about
those Swordquest games?

1129
01:20:24.692 --> 01:20:26.586
Yes!
The Swordquest games.

1130
01:20:26.588 --> 01:20:28.748
They were created for a contest
Atari held with real...

1131
01:20:36.331 --> 01:20:39.331
i-R0k, how are we doin'?

1132
01:20:39.334 --> 01:20:41.604
To be honest, I think I need
physical therapy because it's not...

1133
01:20:41.605 --> 01:20:43.673
Is the Orb ready?

1134
01:20:44.606 --> 01:20:46.336
Um, as you wish.

1135
01:20:50.445 --> 01:20:51.605
The Orb...

1136
01:20:51.613 --> 01:20:53.083
Of Osuvox.

1137
01:20:53.882 --> 01:20:55.049
Ah...

1138
01:20:55.050 --> 01:20:57.117
How does it work?

1139
01:20:57.118 --> 01:21:00.558
Has it got, like, a remote or
is there a button or something?

1140
01:21:00.559 --> 01:21:04.185
Nolan, it's a level-99
magic artifact,

1141
01:21:04.192 --> 01:21:07.999
not one of your drones,
so it is activated by a magic spell.

1142
01:21:08.000 --> 01:21:10.096
Would you care
to do the honors?

1143
01:22:02.017 --> 01:22:03.384
Where is she?

1144
01:22:03.385 --> 01:22:04.685
How'd you get in here?

1145
01:22:04.686 --> 01:22:05.946
- Art3mis.
- Who?

1146
01:22:05.954 --> 01:22:10.624
Samantha Cook. Where is she?

1147
01:22:10.625 --> 01:22:14.525
If you wanna talk, we can talk,
but you gotta put that gun down.

1148
01:22:14.529 --> 01:22:17.429
You killed my mom's sister.

1149
01:22:17.432 --> 01:22:19.072
You think I won't kill you?

1150
01:22:19.073 --> 01:22:23.267
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Just slow down, okay?

1151
01:22:23.271 --> 01:22:26.640
That was a corporate decision.
It was not personal.

1152
01:22:26.641 --> 01:22:27.975
Where is she?

1153
01:22:27.976 --> 01:22:30.306
She's downstairs
in the loyalty center!

1154
01:22:30.312 --> 01:22:33.647
I know she's in
the goddamn loyalty center.

1155
01:22:33.648 --> 01:22:36.118
You're gonna tell me
exactly which rig she's in

1156
01:22:36.119 --> 01:22:38.517
and the access code
to contact her.

1157
01:22:39.554 --> 01:22:41.864
Yeah, that seems appropriate.

1158
01:22:44.659 --> 01:22:46.729
Start with access code.

1159
01:22:47.896 --> 01:22:50.164
6, 45, 7, 25.

1160
01:22:50.165 --> 01:22:51.495
Where's the rig?

1161
01:23:02.344 --> 01:23:04.578
I think he pissed himself.

1162
01:23:04.579 --> 01:23:06.579
Good job, Z.
We're in his account.

1163
01:23:06.581 --> 01:23:08.381
So he really doesn't know
he's in the OASIS?

1164
01:23:10.685 --> 01:23:13.285
This is what Sorrento
should be seeing,

1165
01:23:13.288 --> 01:23:17.524
but this... This is what we're
making him see.

1166
01:23:17.525 --> 01:23:20.594
We grabbed him in transit just as
he was logging out of the OASIS,

1167
01:23:20.595 --> 01:23:23.464
so he thinks he's back in his
office in the real world.

1168
01:23:23.465 --> 01:23:27.295
But actually, he's here, in the
identical office that Aech built.

1169
01:23:27.302 --> 01:23:30.009
So, you basically
just remotely hacked his rig.

1170
01:23:30.010 --> 01:23:33.035
A fixed rig like Sorrento's
is easy to locate, hard to hack.

1171
01:23:33.041 --> 01:23:35.781
Unless he's stupid enough to
leave his password lying around.

1172
01:23:35.782 --> 01:23:37.177
Loyalty center, I'm in.

1173
01:23:37.178 --> 01:23:39.008
All right,
let's get to work.

1174
01:23:46.721 --> 01:23:49.056
- Arty.
- Z? Z? Z?

1175
01:23:49.057 --> 01:23:50.626
Arty, don't say anything.

1176
01:23:50.627 --> 01:23:52.625
I'm tapped directly
into your audio feed.

1177
01:23:54.195 --> 01:23:55.695
How did you find me?

1178
01:23:55.697 --> 01:23:57.467
We got his password,
hacked Sorrento's rig.

1179
01:23:59.034 --> 01:24:01.502
Z, I have something
to tell you.

1180
01:24:01.503 --> 01:24:03.513
Not now. I have something to show
you that'll get you out of there.

1181
01:24:03.514 --> 01:24:06.974
The Sixers found the third challenge.
It's on Planet Doom.

1182
01:24:06.975 --> 01:24:08.505
And there's more,
they just put a force field

1183
01:24:08.510 --> 01:24:10.380
around Anorak's Castle.

1184
01:24:14.749 --> 01:24:17.418
I heard one of the guards
calling it "the Orb of Osuvox,"

1185
01:24:17.419 --> 01:24:19.989
and the only way to take it
down is from the inside.

1186
01:24:19.990 --> 01:24:23.157
She's right.
Level-99 artifact,

1187
01:24:23.158 --> 01:24:26.088
creates a magic-resistant,
impenetrable barrier.

1188
01:24:26.094 --> 01:24:27.828
No way through it.

1189
01:24:27.829 --> 01:24:29.559
Okay, listen.
That's not important right now.

1190
01:24:29.564 --> 01:24:31.564
What's important is that
we get you out of the rig.

1191
01:24:33.701 --> 01:24:36.071
All right, so I'm looking
at a diagram of your rig.

1192
01:24:38.740 --> 01:24:41.175
If you reach up with your
left hand at 11 o'clock,

1193
01:24:41.176 --> 01:24:43.056
there's some... there's a
panel above your head.

1194
01:24:47.749 --> 01:24:49.917
Yeah, yeah.
Yeah, I can feel it.

1195
01:24:49.918 --> 01:24:51.948
Okay, there should be
two release handles.

1196
01:24:51.953 --> 01:24:53.593
Nine o'clock and three o'clock.
Can you feel them?

1197
01:24:53.594 --> 01:24:55.858
- Yeah, I got it.
- Okay, pull it towards you.

1198
01:24:58.193 --> 01:25:00.099
Okay, inside the panel,
there's a lever.

1199
01:25:00.100 --> 01:25:02.455
Grab it with your right hand
and slide it to the left.

1200
01:25:02.464 --> 01:25:03.974
That should release you.

1201
01:25:11.239 --> 01:25:13.974
It worked. It worked, I'm out.

1202
01:25:13.975 --> 01:25:16.105
Loyalty pod 41-F,

1203
01:25:16.111 --> 01:25:19.111
you are on an authorized
break for 10 minutes.

1204
01:25:24.385 --> 01:25:27.554
Pod 41-F, you are
on 10-minute break.

1205
01:25:27.555 --> 01:25:29.715
Proceed to break area.

1206
01:25:30.959 --> 01:25:32.328
Wade, are you still there?

1207
01:25:32.329 --> 01:25:33.557
Yeah, I'm here. Where are you?

1208
01:25:33.561 --> 01:25:35.761
Where is Sorrento's office?

1209
01:25:35.763 --> 01:25:37.173
It's in the IOI war room,
two levels above where you are now.

1210
01:25:37.174 --> 01:25:38.965
But that's not the way out.

1211
01:25:38.967 --> 01:25:40.567
What's his password?

1212
01:25:41.836 --> 01:25:43.236
Wade, answer me.

1213
01:25:43.238 --> 01:25:47.174
Okay, it's capital
B-0-55-man-69.

1214
01:25:47.175 --> 01:25:49.575
But, Arty, you need to go.

1215
01:25:49.577 --> 01:25:50.907
You need to raise an army.

1216
01:25:51.779 --> 01:25:53.409
An army?

1217
01:25:53.414 --> 01:25:55.024
Get to Planet Doom,
and wait for my signal.

1218
01:25:55.025 --> 01:25:56.316
What signal?

1219
01:25:56.317 --> 01:25:58.447
I'm gonna take down
that shield.

1220
01:25:58.453 --> 01:26:00.453
Wait, Arty, wait!
You gotta get out of there! Arty!

1221
01:26:08.796 --> 01:26:11.426
Hey, how much
are they paying you?

1222
01:26:11.432 --> 01:26:13.202
'Cause, man, I got a lot of paper.

1223
01:26:13.203 --> 01:26:15.601
You know, I can make you,
like, a forest.

1224
01:26:15.603 --> 01:26:17.871
Hey, shut up.

1225
01:26:17.872 --> 01:26:19.042
Okay.

1226
01:26:41.629 --> 01:26:43.869
This isn't real,
you're tapping my feed.

1227
01:26:43.870 --> 01:26:45.925
Uh-oh. Guys.

1228
01:27:04.419 --> 01:27:07.159
F'Nale, they've hacked my rig.
They're after the girl.

1229
01:27:07.160 --> 01:27:09.415
Meet me at loyalty.

1230
01:27:22.937 --> 01:27:26.537
Pod 41-F,
you have exceeded your break time.

1231
01:27:26.541 --> 01:27:30.311
Report to security or your coin
count will be reset to zero.

1232
01:27:39.220 --> 01:27:44.024
So, she just walks out of here,
how does that happen?

1233
01:27:44.025 --> 01:27:46.285
They're smart. They knew
what they were doing.

1234
01:27:46.294 --> 01:27:49.134
But we know they're in Columbus. And now,
all five of them are together.

1235
01:27:49.135 --> 01:27:51.630
Wait. Wait, we know what?
How do we know?

1236
01:27:51.633 --> 01:27:55.402
We have the make and model of the van.
We'll spot them.

1237
01:27:55.403 --> 01:27:57.537
"We'll spot them"?

1238
01:27:57.538 --> 01:28:00.777
That sounds like a great
inscription for our tombstones.

1239
01:28:00.778 --> 01:28:02.305
Why didn't you tell me
this earlier?

1240
01:28:02.310 --> 01:28:03.910
It wasn't relevant yet.

1241
01:28:03.911 --> 01:28:05.311
I need to know where they are.

1242
01:28:05.313 --> 01:28:06.713
We need to know.
We need to find them!

1243
01:28:06.714 --> 01:28:09.750
They're kids, Nolan.
Man the hell up!

1244
01:28:09.751 --> 01:28:12.951
Do your job, and I'll do mine,
unless you wanna take this

1245
01:28:12.954 --> 01:28:15.024
and go after them yourself.

1246
01:28:19.560 --> 01:28:20.860
Find them!

1247
01:28:29.804 --> 01:28:34.484
The Complete Nancy Drew,
Kegel Exercises for...

1248
01:28:36.077 --> 01:28:38.807
Bingo. Okay.

1249
01:28:38.813 --> 01:28:41.083
"Congratulations, you are the
proud owner of the Orb of Osuvox,

1250
01:28:41.084 --> 01:28:43.020
"a 99th level magic artifact.

1251
01:28:43.021 --> 01:28:45.847
"Read these instructions before deploying.
To turn orb on, off."

1252
01:28:45.853 --> 01:28:47.354
Off! Yes, off.

1253
01:28:47.355 --> 01:28:49.685
"Utter spell
within 10 feet of orb."

1254
01:29:03.604 --> 01:29:05.806
Citizens of the OASIS,

1255
01:29:05.807 --> 01:29:08.637
I am Parzival,
first to the key.

1256
01:29:08.643 --> 01:29:11.683
I'm here talking to all of you now
because our future's being threatened

1257
01:29:11.684 --> 01:29:15.779
by people who will stop at
nothing to win this contest.

1258
01:29:15.783 --> 01:29:17.818
Some of you already know this,

1259
01:29:17.819 --> 01:29:21.788
and you've lost much more than
just your avatars or your weapons.

1260
01:29:21.789 --> 01:29:25.729
Some have lost their freedom.
Some have lost their lives.

1261
01:29:28.162 --> 01:29:30.964
And now, this.

1262
01:29:30.965 --> 01:29:33.965
A force field
around the third challenge.

1263
01:29:36.471 --> 01:29:40.481
I only came here to escape the
shitty hand that life dealt me.

1264
01:29:40.482 --> 01:29:43.235
But I stayed,
like many of you,

1265
01:29:43.244 --> 01:29:48.348
because I found something
much bigger than just myself.

1266
01:29:48.349 --> 01:29:50.219
I found a cause.

1267
01:29:51.319 --> 01:29:54.588
I found my friends.

1268
01:29:54.589 --> 01:29:58.089
And yes, I know
it's kind of a groaner, but...

1269
01:29:59.360 --> 01:30:01.000
I found love.

1270
01:30:02.230 --> 01:30:03.868
And I don't wanna lose that

1271
01:30:03.869 --> 01:30:06.525
to this colossal douchebag,
Nolan Sorrento.

1272
01:30:06.534 --> 01:30:10.737
This guy.
Back to work, people.

1273
01:30:10.738 --> 01:30:15.008
He thinks that we're all too
distracted to even notice...

1274
01:30:15.009 --> 01:30:19.779
Nolan Sorrento thinks
that we won't put up a fight.

1275
01:30:19.781 --> 01:30:21.047
Sir! Sir!

1276
01:30:21.048 --> 01:30:22.848
This is going out live!

1277
01:30:22.850 --> 01:30:24.950
The only thing
Halliday let this guy do...

1278
01:30:24.952 --> 01:30:26.620
- It's absolutely everywhere.
- ...was get him a cup of coffee.

1279
01:30:26.621 --> 01:30:28.421
And now, we're supposed
to hand him the OASIS?

1280
01:30:35.396 --> 01:30:38.196
This Parzival...
Oh, man.

1281
01:30:42.236 --> 01:30:44.736
Come on, come on.
Give me this thing.

1282
01:30:44.739 --> 01:30:45.939
Yes, sir.

1283
01:30:46.574 --> 01:30:48.708
Left arm.

1284
01:30:48.709 --> 01:30:51.209
- Left arm!
- Sir.

1285
01:30:51.212 --> 01:30:53.212
No, I need the left arm.

1286
01:30:53.214 --> 01:30:55.554
No, I don't care if...
I want it on.

1287
01:30:57.385 --> 01:31:00.145
He thinks that we
won't even put up a fight!

1288
01:31:00.154 --> 01:31:02.956
Well, I say he's wrong.

1289
01:31:02.957 --> 01:31:06.757
I say, tell that to the gunter
clans in the gold mines of Gygax.

1290
01:31:06.761 --> 01:31:10.001
Activate the Iron Giant.

1291
01:31:34.088 --> 01:31:39.158
Ask yourselves, are you willing
to zero out for the OASIS?

1292
01:31:39.160 --> 01:31:41.100
Are you willing to fight?

1293
01:31:42.497 --> 01:31:45.097
I am Parzival
of the High Five.

1294
01:31:45.099 --> 01:31:47.839
In the name of Art3mis,
in the name of Aech,

1295
01:31:47.840 --> 01:31:50.535
in the name of Daito and Sho,

1296
01:31:50.538 --> 01:31:54.107
we ask you to join us
on Planet Doom.

1297
01:31:54.108 --> 01:31:57.208
In the name
of James Halliday himself,

1298
01:31:57.211 --> 01:31:59.281
help us save the OASIS.

1299
01:32:54.235 --> 01:32:56.665
No, no, no, no.

1300
01:33:06.747 --> 01:33:09.377
"No man is a failure
who has friends."

1301
01:33:31.472 --> 01:33:34.712
Squadron 14, armor up,
you're in the lead.

1302
01:33:47.588 --> 01:33:51.988
One minute into Swordquest,
the ice broke.

1303
01:33:51.993 --> 01:33:55.762
Well, all three Swordquests.
What's next?

1304
01:33:55.763 --> 01:33:57.603
Dark Cavern, Laser Blast.

1305
01:33:57.604 --> 01:33:58.828
It's Adventure.

1306
01:33:58.833 --> 01:34:01.101
Released in 1979,
for the 2600,

1307
01:34:01.102 --> 01:34:03.169
Adventure was created by
Warren Robinett,

1308
01:34:03.170 --> 01:34:05.340
who was the first video game designer
ever to hide his name. In fact...

1309
01:34:05.341 --> 01:34:07.409
Try Adventure.

1310
01:34:08.609 --> 01:34:10.179
Play Adventure.

1311
01:35:02.496 --> 01:35:04.826
More than a minute,
we're still alive.

1312
01:35:04.832 --> 01:35:06.866
This must be the right game.

1313
01:35:13.641 --> 01:35:16.481
How long does it last,
this orb thing?

1314
01:35:23.884 --> 01:35:26.653
I'd say about ten...

1315
01:35:26.654 --> 01:35:30.023
Yeah, about 10 million years,
so we should be fine.

1316
01:35:47.208 --> 01:35:49.075
First to the key!

1317
01:35:49.076 --> 01:35:50.906
First to the egg!

1318
01:35:50.911 --> 01:35:53.780
First to the egg!

1319
01:35:53.781 --> 01:35:57.016
♪ We're not gonna take it

1320
01:35:57.017 --> 01:36:00.386
♪ No, we ain't gonna take it

1321
01:36:00.387 --> 01:36:04.827
♪ We're not
gonna take it anymore

1322
01:36:10.431 --> 01:36:13.366
♪ We've got the right
to choose it

1323
01:36:13.367 --> 01:36:16.697
♪ There ain't no way
we'll lose it

1324
01:36:16.704 --> 01:36:19.214
♪ This is our life,
this is our song

1325
01:36:22.109 --> 01:36:23.739
Adventure.

1326
01:36:23.744 --> 01:36:26.479
♪ We'll fight the powers
that be just

1327
01:36:26.480 --> 01:36:29.580
♪ Don't pick
our destiny 'cause

1328
01:36:29.583 --> 01:36:32.418
♪ You don't know us,
you don't belong

1329
01:36:39.627 --> 01:36:41.897
What? Come on!

1330
01:36:52.239 --> 01:36:55.475
♪ Your gall is never-ending

1331
01:36:55.476 --> 01:36:59.006
♪ We don't want nothin'
Not a thing from you ♪

1332
01:37:11.458 --> 01:37:13.088
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

1333
01:37:15.196 --> 01:37:17.966
The Sixers are in the final challenge.
It's an Atari 2600.

1334
01:37:17.967 --> 01:37:20.195
Are you in the Sixer war room?

1335
01:37:20.201 --> 01:37:21.801
No, no, no.
You gotta get out of there.

1336
01:37:21.802 --> 01:37:24.102
They're playing Adventure.

1337
01:37:24.104 --> 01:37:26.506
Adventure, of course!

1338
01:37:26.507 --> 01:37:28.307
Created by Warren Robinett!

1339
01:37:28.309 --> 01:37:29.839
He was the first designer to
ever hide an Easter egg in...

1340
01:37:29.844 --> 01:37:30.914
Dude!

1341
01:37:35.883 --> 01:37:38.723
We're looking for a USPS truck,
Ohio plates,

1342
01:37:38.724 --> 01:37:41.789
a drone spitter, 2036 model.

1343
01:38:00.307 --> 01:38:03.707
Daito! When are you
getting into this fight?

1344
01:38:17.658 --> 01:38:18.888
I'm out. Inventory's empty.

1345
01:38:18.893 --> 01:38:20.059
Last clip for me.

1346
01:38:20.060 --> 01:38:21.260
More weapons!

1347
01:38:21.262 --> 01:38:25.432
Anti-personnel
ordinance cannon!

1348
01:38:28.335 --> 01:38:31.065
Railgun!

1349
01:38:36.210 --> 01:38:37.910
Yo, Z!

1350
01:38:37.912 --> 01:38:41.622
Yo, Z! Try this little guy.

1351
01:38:45.119 --> 01:38:46.786
Ow!

1352
01:38:46.787 --> 01:38:48.687
Get rid of it! Get rid of it!

1353
01:38:49.757 --> 01:38:51.624
It's fucking Chucky!

1354
01:38:56.897 --> 01:38:58.965
Move! Move!

1355
01:38:58.966 --> 01:39:00.526
Go, go, go!

1356
01:39:58.258 --> 01:39:59.826
Mechagodzilla!

1357
01:40:20.948 --> 01:40:24.448
Daito, we need you!
Daito, now!

1358
01:40:24.451 --> 01:40:26.691
Get to the bridge.
Go now, he's distracted.

1359
01:40:26.692 --> 01:40:27.757
Go, go, go.

1360
01:41:09.029 --> 01:41:10.099
Z!

1361
01:41:29.950 --> 01:41:31.750
Arty!

1362
01:41:31.752 --> 01:41:33.792
Get to the castle!
Win the third key before they do!

1363
01:41:45.065 --> 01:41:46.765
What is that?

1364
01:41:46.767 --> 01:41:49.197
He's only got 30 seconds
before changing back!

1365
01:42:00.380 --> 01:42:03.320
Daito, abort, abort!
You got 10 seconds!

1366
01:42:17.931 --> 01:42:19.201
First to the egg!

1367
01:42:58.605 --> 01:42:59.935
Shit, it's her.

1368
01:43:19.960 --> 01:43:23.296
Arty! Arty!

1369
01:43:23.297 --> 01:43:25.827
Z! Got to get
to the castle!

1370
01:43:31.838 --> 01:43:34.468
She never left.
She's still here.

1371
01:43:37.377 --> 01:43:38.977
The girl's in the war room.

1372
01:44:17.050 --> 01:44:18.650
No, no, no.

1373
01:44:32.733 --> 01:44:35.343
Sho! Hang on!

1374
01:44:54.721 --> 01:44:56.361
No!

1375
01:45:18.779 --> 01:45:20.679
Arty, we've got this.
You need to log out.

1376
01:45:20.681 --> 01:45:23.451
If the game is Adventure,
why haven't they won yet?

1377
01:45:23.452 --> 01:45:25.318
I don't know. Arty, Arty.

1378
01:45:25.319 --> 01:45:27.319
I'm serious, Sorrento's crazy.
He'll kill you.

1379
01:45:29.489 --> 01:45:31.457
What are you looking at?

1380
01:45:31.458 --> 01:45:33.258
There's nothing over there.

1381
01:45:34.261 --> 01:45:35.461
You're in trouble, aren't you?

1382
01:45:38.699 --> 01:45:42.268
Samantha, you know I love you.

1383
01:45:42.269 --> 01:45:43.636
Not the time, Z.

1384
01:45:43.637 --> 01:45:45.206
I can handle the challenge,

1385
01:45:45.207 --> 01:45:48.174
but I can't let you get hurt
in the real world.

1386
01:45:48.175 --> 01:45:51.405
Get out of IOI,
and meet us at River South.

1387
01:45:57.718 --> 01:45:59.448
Wade, no.

1388
01:45:59.453 --> 01:46:01.323
You'll forgive me
for this, I promise.

1389
01:46:01.324 --> 01:46:02.521
Wade, no, no, no.

1390
01:46:12.566 --> 01:46:16.035
Get it together, Sixer.
Back to respawn.

1391
01:46:16.036 --> 01:46:17.366
Let's go, move.

1392
01:46:17.371 --> 01:46:18.641
You're in.

1393
01:46:36.857 --> 01:46:39.487
Holy hand grenade!
How much did that cost?

1394
01:46:39.493 --> 01:46:42.003
Less than
it's gonna cost them.

1395
01:46:43.063 --> 01:46:44.633
What is that?

1396
01:46:54.941 --> 01:46:57.681
Sir, the gunters
are approaching the challenge.

1397
01:46:57.682 --> 01:46:59.677
- i-R0k?
- In position, sir.

1398
01:46:59.679 --> 01:47:00.946
Prepare my rig.

1399
01:47:00.947 --> 01:47:03.647
The ice is holding.
Still going.

1400
01:47:13.927 --> 01:47:15.257
Wait.

1401
01:47:15.262 --> 01:47:16.462
He's trying to win.

1402
01:47:19.766 --> 01:47:22.366
Yeah! I won.

1403
01:47:25.806 --> 01:47:27.766
He lost.

1404
01:47:27.774 --> 01:47:29.844
Not Adventure.

1405
01:47:33.914 --> 01:47:38.384
Everyone who wins loses.

1406
01:47:38.385 --> 01:47:41.715
It's not about winning.
It's about playing.

1407
01:47:42.789 --> 01:47:45.289
Remember
Halliday's announcement.

1408
01:47:45.292 --> 01:47:47.732
The keys are invisible,
and they're hidden in a dark room

1409
01:47:47.733 --> 01:47:50.296
that's at the center
of a maze.

1410
01:47:50.297 --> 01:47:53.966
Well, there's a secret in Adventure,
and you don't find it by winning.

1411
01:47:53.967 --> 01:47:56.897
You find it by wandering
around in a dark room.

1412
01:47:56.903 --> 01:47:58.604
Until you get
to the invisible dot.

1413
01:47:58.605 --> 01:48:00.305
It's pretty easy
if you know what you're doing.

1414
01:48:00.307 --> 01:48:01.637
Really?

1415
01:48:02.476 --> 01:48:04.844
Let me finish it for you.

1416
01:48:08.815 --> 01:48:10.745
It's your last chance, Wade.

1417
01:48:10.750 --> 01:48:13.650
Last chance. Give me the key.

1418
01:48:13.653 --> 01:48:18.691
I give you 50 million
in your account right now.

1419
01:48:18.692 --> 01:48:20.532
Why the hell
would I ever do that?

1420
01:48:22.262 --> 01:48:24.200
Dude!
That's the Cataclyst.

1421
01:48:24.201 --> 01:48:26.097
Now, personally, I don't care.

1422
01:48:26.099 --> 01:48:27.829
I'd just as soon never set
foot in the OASIS again,

1423
01:48:27.834 --> 01:48:30.004
let alone have to deal
with any of this absurdity.

1424
01:48:30.005 --> 01:48:35.207
But I know how important Halliday's
competition is to you, so...

1425
01:48:35.208 --> 01:48:39.648
I will never let the future of the OASIS
rest in your hands, Nolan Sorrento.

1426
01:48:39.649 --> 01:48:43.676
Well, that's fine.
Three easy steps. One.

1427
01:48:43.683 --> 01:48:46.153
Wait, I thought you were bluffing.
You know that kills all of us, right?

1428
01:48:46.154 --> 01:48:48.222
I've got 10 years' worth
of shit inside of me.

1429
01:48:48.223 --> 01:48:49.889
Last chance. Two.

1430
01:48:49.890 --> 01:48:51.290
I'm not goin' out like that.

1431
01:48:51.291 --> 01:48:52.825
That's a camper move.

1432
01:48:52.826 --> 01:48:54.506
You don't even know
how to activate an orb.

1433
01:49:06.139 --> 01:49:07.269
Yeah, I felt those.

1434
01:49:08.642 --> 01:49:10.782
But this is my world,
Sorrento.

1435
01:49:14.681 --> 01:49:15.981
Hadouken!

1436
01:49:35.535 --> 01:49:38.165
- No, no, no!
- Step three.

1437
01:49:38.171 --> 01:49:39.941
No, no, no!

1438
01:50:37.397 --> 01:50:39.127
Get me out of this thing.

1439
01:50:53.513 --> 01:50:54.947
Uh...

1440
01:50:54.948 --> 01:50:56.248
Guys?

1441
01:51:02.789 --> 01:51:04.689
Z. He's still alive!

1442
01:51:12.532 --> 01:51:14.402
Extra life.

1443
01:51:16.770 --> 01:51:18.240
Thanks, Curator.

1444
01:51:21.041 --> 01:51:22.241
Hold on.

1445
01:51:29.949 --> 01:51:32.549
Live feed
in all OASIS channels.

1446
01:51:32.552 --> 01:51:35.159
Halliday's letting everyone
watch the end of the contest.

1447
01:51:35.160 --> 01:51:36.515
That's so Halliday.

1448
01:51:36.523 --> 01:51:38.791
God damn it,
we tried Adventure.

1449
01:51:38.792 --> 01:51:40.359
No, we tried to win it.

1450
01:51:40.360 --> 01:51:42.830
But the hidden room isn't
at the end of the game.

1451
01:51:42.831 --> 01:51:45.399
You've gotta go straight
to the invisible dot at the start.

1452
01:51:59.012 --> 01:52:00.979
Is that her?

1453
01:52:00.980 --> 01:52:04.380
Red hair, IOI uniform,
doesn't know what planet she's on?

1454
01:52:04.384 --> 01:52:05.494
That's her.

1455
01:52:17.263 --> 01:52:20.073
I'm Toshiro.
You know me as Daito.

1456
01:52:22.902 --> 01:52:24.002
Oh.

1457
01:52:26.706 --> 01:52:28.166
Hey, Arty.

1458
01:52:30.176 --> 01:52:34.346
Yeah, I know. Not what
you were expecting, huh?

1459
01:52:34.347 --> 01:52:38.947
Yeah, I wasn't expecting
a late '30s-model postal van.

1460
01:52:40.954 --> 01:52:43.122
Wade?

1461
01:52:43.123 --> 01:52:45.093
Wait, I thought the Cataclyst went off.
How are you still playing?

1462
01:52:45.094 --> 01:52:47.661
Extra life, long story.
Sorry I shot you.

1463
01:52:49.929 --> 01:52:51.559
Sho?

1464
01:52:51.564 --> 01:52:54.102
What? Do I have to wear
a sign saying,

1465
01:52:54.103 --> 01:52:57.239
"I am 11 years old, shoot me first"?
No, thanks.

1466
01:52:57.240 --> 01:52:59.567
- Dude, give me a hug.
- Ninjas don't hug!

1467
01:52:59.572 --> 01:53:01.252
All right, everybody,
hold on to somethin'.

1468
01:53:22.896 --> 01:53:24.226
Got you.

1469
01:53:27.934 --> 01:53:29.704
Come on, Nolan. Pick up.

1470
01:53:31.838 --> 01:53:34.668
F'Nale, tell me
something good.

1471
01:53:34.674 --> 01:53:37.244
I've got a drone on their tail.
I'm close.

1472
01:53:37.245 --> 01:53:38.512
Send me coordinates.

1473
01:53:38.513 --> 01:53:40.751
Maybe you should
leave this to me, Nolan.

1474
01:53:42.515 --> 01:53:45.185
Nolan? Nolan.

1475
01:53:46.586 --> 01:53:47.746
Out.

1476
01:53:56.663 --> 01:53:59.203
Give me that.

1477
01:54:02.836 --> 01:54:04.596
What's goin' on out there?

1478
01:54:08.942 --> 01:54:11.442
The game is over for them.
What are they watching?

1479
01:54:13.880 --> 01:54:16.250
The final key!
It's being broadcast.

1480
01:54:18.284 --> 01:54:19.952
You see,

1481
01:54:19.953 --> 01:54:22.654
Warren Robinett
was proud of Adventure.

1482
01:54:22.655 --> 01:54:25.724
He wanted people to know
who was behind it.

1483
01:54:25.725 --> 01:54:28.455
That's why he created
the first digital Easter egg

1484
01:54:28.461 --> 01:54:31.161
and to find it,
you didn't even have to win.

1485
01:54:31.164 --> 01:54:35.334
You just had to blindly play,
searching around

1486
01:54:35.335 --> 01:54:39.465
in rooms for an invisible dot.

1487
01:54:39.472 --> 01:54:42.042
You took the dot
back to the main screen

1488
01:54:42.043 --> 01:54:46.680
and that's when you found the first
Easter egg ever put in a video game.

1489
01:54:46.681 --> 01:54:47.979
The creator's name.

1490
01:55:12.605 --> 01:55:14.705
What's going on, man?
I can't see shit.

1491
01:55:14.707 --> 01:55:16.137
Parzival just got
the Crystal Key!

1492
01:55:31.391 --> 01:55:33.161
Do you want it or not?

1493
01:55:36.429 --> 01:55:38.529
Aech,
what the hell's going on?

1494
01:55:38.531 --> 01:55:40.531
Just practicing Mario Kart.
What do you think?

1495
01:55:40.533 --> 01:55:42.643
IOI's trying to kill us, man!

1496
01:55:56.816 --> 01:55:59.146
Everyone watching,
if you're in the Columbus stacks,

1497
01:55:59.152 --> 01:56:01.219
this is Parzival.

1498
01:56:01.220 --> 01:56:03.420
My real-world name is Wade Watts,
and we're gonna need your help.

1499
01:56:03.423 --> 01:56:04.993
Aech, head for the stacks!

1500
01:56:04.994 --> 01:56:07.259
Okay, hold on!

1501
01:56:31.918 --> 01:56:33.918
Stick the key in,
how hard is it?

1502
01:56:39.592 --> 01:56:40.832
Come on.

1503
01:56:48.201 --> 01:56:50.271
Yeah! Yes!

1504
01:57:06.452 --> 01:57:07.722
That's it?

1505
01:57:08.488 --> 01:57:10.355
Yeah, that's it.

1506
01:57:10.356 --> 01:57:14.856
Now, you just sign these papers,
and the OASIS is yours.

1507
01:57:14.861 --> 01:57:19.164
You will be
its sole proprietor.

1508
01:57:19.165 --> 01:57:20.695
That ain't so bad, is it?

1509
01:57:42.488 --> 01:57:43.588
I'm gonna need a second.

1510
01:58:12.218 --> 01:58:14.848
This is wrong.

1511
01:58:14.854 --> 01:58:17.794
This pen, this contract.

1512
01:58:20.960 --> 01:58:22.730
This is the moment
that Halliday made Morrow

1513
01:58:22.731 --> 01:58:25.297
sign over his shares
in Gregarious.

1514
01:58:25.298 --> 01:58:27.968
That was the biggest mistake
of his life.

1515
01:58:27.969 --> 01:58:30.167
He knew that.

1516
01:58:31.871 --> 01:58:33.971
This can't be the end.

1517
01:58:35.108 --> 01:58:36.878
It's a test.

1518
01:58:41.380 --> 01:58:44.120
I won't make
the same mistake you did.

1519
01:58:49.755 --> 01:58:51.685
Oh, good.

1520
01:58:54.327 --> 01:58:57.827
I just needed to be sure.

1521
01:59:11.777 --> 01:59:14.047
This is where you grew up.

1522
01:59:23.256 --> 01:59:26.186
Oh, that's just me
a long time ago.

1523
01:59:26.192 --> 01:59:29.794
I like to have him around
from time to time.

1524
01:59:29.795 --> 01:59:32.095
Hey, I have
to show you something.

1525
01:59:32.098 --> 01:59:33.798
This, uh... Come on.

1526
01:59:33.799 --> 01:59:35.634
This is the button.

1527
01:59:35.635 --> 01:59:38.935
If you push it, the whole
simulation shuts down

1528
01:59:38.938 --> 01:59:42.538
and a tapeworm program will erase
all of the backup servers.

1529
01:59:42.542 --> 01:59:46.311
So you now have the power
to turn the OASIS off forever.

1530
01:59:46.312 --> 01:59:47.952
Do you understand?

1531
01:59:53.319 --> 01:59:54.486
Yeah,

1532
01:59:54.487 --> 01:59:56.454
try not to accidentally erase

1533
01:59:56.455 --> 01:59:59.185
the whole of the OASIS
on your first day.

1534
02:00:08.501 --> 02:00:10.271
The stacks are straight ahead!

1535
02:00:26.018 --> 02:00:28.987
Well, I expect you have to go.
I know I do.

1536
02:00:28.988 --> 02:00:31.518
So, now is the time for you
to receive your prize

1537
02:00:31.524 --> 02:00:34.059
because you won
all three keys.

1538
02:00:34.060 --> 02:00:38.760
Once you take this egg,
the game will be over.

1539
02:00:38.764 --> 02:00:41.904
The egg, the egg...

1540
02:00:49.275 --> 02:00:51.705
We know what you did here.

1541
02:00:51.711 --> 02:00:55.081
You turn around and walk out
of here while you still can.

1542
02:01:07.627 --> 02:01:10.195
I created the OASIS

1543
02:01:10.196 --> 02:01:14.926
because I never felt at home
in the real world.

1544
02:01:14.934 --> 02:01:19.404
I just didn't know how to
connect with the people there.

1545
02:01:19.405 --> 02:01:22.905
I was afraid
for all of my life.

1546
02:01:22.908 --> 02:01:25.708
Right up until the day
I knew my life was ending.

1547
02:01:31.284 --> 02:01:36.288
Now, that... That was when
I realized that,

1548
02:01:36.289 --> 02:01:41.459
as terrifying and painful
as reality can be,

1549
02:01:42.261 --> 02:01:46.331
it's also the only place

1550
02:01:47.933 --> 02:01:49.643
that you can get
a decent meal.

1551
02:01:56.242 --> 02:01:57.812
Because

1552
02:01:59.478 --> 02:02:01.148
reality

1553
02:02:06.252 --> 02:02:07.919
is real.

1554
02:02:07.920 --> 02:02:09.690
You understand
what I'm saying?

1555
02:02:11.457 --> 02:02:14.157
Yes. Yes, I do.

1556
02:02:23.869 --> 02:02:25.199
He did it.

1557
02:02:26.839 --> 02:02:28.369
He got the egg.

1558
02:02:29.141 --> 02:02:30.441
Hooray.

1559
02:02:31.544 --> 02:02:33.254
- No!
- No! Please!

1560
02:03:06.746 --> 02:03:08.076
Hold it!

1561
02:03:10.082 --> 02:03:13.852
Drop the gun! Now!
On the ground!

1562
02:03:13.853 --> 02:03:16.588
Turn around!
Hands on your head.

1563
02:03:16.589 --> 02:03:18.219
Walk back towards me.

1564
02:03:33.873 --> 02:03:39.110
Mr. Halliday.
Something I don't understand.

1565
02:03:39.111 --> 02:03:41.911
You're not an avatar, are you?

1566
02:03:42.448 --> 02:03:44.148
No.

1567
02:03:45.618 --> 02:03:47.688
Is Halliday really dead?

1568
02:03:49.288 --> 02:03:50.958
Yes.

1569
02:03:56.629 --> 02:03:58.459
Then what are you?

1570
02:04:01.634 --> 02:04:03.674
Goodbye, Parzival.

1571
02:04:05.271 --> 02:04:06.441
Thanks.

1572
02:04:07.907 --> 02:04:10.177
Thanks for playing my game.

1573
02:04:39.138 --> 02:04:40.508
Wade?

1574
02:04:41.841 --> 02:04:43.781
- Ogden Morrow?
- Ogden Morrow?

1575
02:04:43.782 --> 02:04:45.944
You can call me "Og."

1576
02:04:45.945 --> 02:04:48.905
Now, there are some people out here
that would very much like to meet you.

1577
02:04:48.914 --> 02:04:52.150
Wow, this is incredible.

1578
02:04:52.151 --> 02:04:54.991
It's an honor to meet you,
Og, but I...

1579
02:04:59.124 --> 02:05:00.864
There's something
I need to do first.

1580
02:05:04.697 --> 02:05:06.527
I'm not like Halliday.

1581
02:05:10.202 --> 02:05:12.342
I'm taking the leap.

1582
02:05:28.721 --> 02:05:31.856
We're looking for Wade Watts.

1583
02:05:31.857 --> 02:05:34.127
We need you to make a statement
about the clip you sent in

1584
02:05:34.128 --> 02:05:36.326
of Nolan Sorrento's
confession.

1585
02:05:36.328 --> 02:05:39.058
Uh, that was me.

1586
02:05:39.064 --> 02:05:41.704
What? I record everything
in my workshop.

1587
02:05:48.040 --> 02:05:49.980
Help me out of this.

1588
02:05:56.248 --> 02:05:58.548
Who are you guys?

1589
02:05:58.551 --> 02:06:02.921
The people you need right now, lawyers.
From Gregarious Games.

1590
02:06:05.691 --> 02:06:07.391
They want
your signature, Wade.

1591
02:06:15.267 --> 02:06:17.535
I'm splitting it with my clan.

1592
02:06:17.536 --> 02:06:19.406
We're gonna
run things together.

1593
02:06:23.876 --> 02:06:26.076
That's a good choice.

1594
02:06:53.872 --> 02:06:57.475
F'Nale, listen to me
very carefully.

1595
02:07:06.118 --> 02:07:09.048
Mr. Morrow... I mean, Og,

1596
02:07:09.054 --> 02:07:10.560
how'd you get here so fast?

1597
02:07:10.561 --> 02:07:13.256
I flew from the stars
on my magic sleigh.

1598
02:07:13.258 --> 02:07:15.827
Everyone's been watching.

1599
02:07:15.828 --> 02:07:19.128
Of course, I've been watching
a little closer than most.

1600
02:07:23.102 --> 02:07:25.002
You?

1601
02:07:25.004 --> 02:07:26.314
You're the Curator?

1602
02:07:29.975 --> 02:07:33.444
Well played, Parzival.

1603
02:07:33.445 --> 02:07:35.475
Jim told me
nothing about the contest,

1604
02:07:35.481 --> 02:07:38.850
so there was no rule about me
losing a bet to a smart kid.

1605
02:07:38.851 --> 02:07:41.486
Not that you needed my help.

1606
02:07:41.487 --> 02:07:45.817
You figured out that Kira
was the key on your own.

1607
02:07:45.824 --> 02:07:48.534
Yeah, but...
Kira wasn't the key.

1608
02:07:49.795 --> 02:07:51.725
It was you, Mr. Morrow.

1609
02:07:53.799 --> 02:07:55.629
You were the Rosebud.

1610
02:07:55.634 --> 02:07:57.904
And Halliday's
biggest regret was

1611
02:07:59.538 --> 02:08:01.208
losing his only friend.

1612
02:08:05.377 --> 02:08:07.707
You know,
Jim used to say the OASIS

1613
02:08:07.713 --> 02:08:10.253
was never supposed to be
a one-player game.

1614
02:08:13.886 --> 02:08:16.686
Now, who do we have here?

1615
02:08:16.689 --> 02:08:19.357
Oh. Well, look who it is.

1616
02:08:19.358 --> 02:08:21.127
It's my heroes, the High Five.

1617
02:08:21.128 --> 02:08:22.796
- You must be Art3mis.
- Samantha.

1618
02:08:22.797 --> 02:08:24.725
The High Five
took over the OASIS,

1619
02:08:24.730 --> 02:08:26.630
and the first thing we did

1620
02:08:26.632 --> 02:08:29.872
was sign Ogden Morrow to
a non-exclusive consultancy.

1621
02:08:29.873 --> 02:08:32.868
The salary, per his demand,

1622
02:08:32.871 --> 02:08:36.140
was 25 cents. One quarter.

1623
02:08:39.344 --> 02:08:41.754
With his guidance,
our second move was to ban

1624
02:08:41.755 --> 02:08:45.216
any loyalty centers
from accessing the OASIS.

1625
02:08:45.217 --> 02:08:48.717
IOI had no choice.
They shut 'em all down.

1626
02:08:51.423 --> 02:08:54.425
The third thing we did
wasn't as popular.

1627
02:08:54.426 --> 02:08:58.426
We closed the OASIS
on Tuesdays and Thursdays.

1628
02:08:58.430 --> 02:09:00.930
I know, it sounds
like a weird move,

1629
02:09:00.933 --> 02:09:03.903
but people need to spend
more time in the real world.

1630
02:09:05.504 --> 02:09:08.573
'Cause, like Halliday said,

1631
02:09:08.574 --> 02:09:12.984
reality is the only thing
that's real.
